1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:02,700
No more thinking tonight.

2
00:00:03,940 --> 00:00:08,440
Nothing you decide at this hour will be
better than what you decide tomorrow.

3
00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:15,100
For the next few hours it's just the
Gospel of Matthew, read slowly.

4
00:00:16,380 --> 00:00:17,540
Let it go past you.

5
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:19,380
Close your eyes.

6
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:25,700
If there's something you'd like prayed over
tonight, leave it below — this comment section

7
00:00:25,740 --> 00:00:29,020
is a quiet one, and people pray through
it.

8
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:31,840
Subscribe if you'd like the next reading.

9
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:38,580
God, it's late, and I'm still deciding
things that don't need deciding tonight.

10
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:40,760
Some of them are real.

11
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:48,100
Most of them are rehearsals —
conversations I'll never have, arranged and rearranged

12
00:00:48,140 --> 00:00:49,460
until they're worn smooth.

13
00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:51,600
I'd like to stop.

14
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:53,020
Not permanently.

15
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:54,860
Just until morning.

16
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,700
You gave the day its own troubles and told
us that was enough.

17
00:01:00,380 --> 00:01:07,100
I've been trying to take on tomorrow's share
as well, in the dark, alone, with none of

18
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:08,240
the facts I'd need.

19
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:10,240
That's not diligence.

20
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:13,080
It's just fear moving quickly.

21
00:01:14,060 --> 00:01:16,060
So let me hear your Son instead.

22
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:22,780
Let his teaching be the thing my mind runs
on for the next few hours, until it forgets

23
00:01:22,820 --> 00:01:23,720
to run at all.

24
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:25,920
Take the decisions off the table.

25
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:27,600
They'll keep.

26
00:01:27,860 --> 00:01:29,900
Keep this house through the night.

27
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:33,800
Keep the people I'd worry about if I let
myself.

28
00:01:34,700 --> 00:01:41,460
And when morning comes, let me meet it
rested, and one step behind you rather than

29
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:43,040
three steps ahead of myself.

30
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:04,200
Amen.

31
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:04,705
Matthew, chapter one.

32
00:02:04,745 --> 00:02:07,400
The book of the genealogy of Jesus Christ,
the son of David, the son of Abraham.

33
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:08,411
Abraham became the father of Isaac.

34
00:02:08,451 --> 00:02:09,421
Isaac became the father of Jacob.

35
00:02:09,461 --> 00:02:10,937
Jacob became the father of Judah and his
brothers.

36
00:02:10,977 --> 00:02:12,621
Judah became the father of Perez and Zerah
by Tamar.

37
00:02:12,661 --> 00:02:13,632
Perez became the father of Hezron.

38
00:02:13,672 --> 00:02:15,300
Hezron became the father of Ram.

39
00:02:16,340 --> 00:02:19,070
Ram became the father of Amminadab.

40
00:02:19,110 --> 00:02:22,320
Amminadab became the father of Nahshon.

41
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:25,260
Nahshon became the father of Salmon.

42
00:02:25,300 --> 00:02:28,860
Salmon became the father of Boaz by Rahab.

43
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:32,320
Boaz became the father of Obed by Ruth.

44
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:35,020
Obed became the father of Jesse.

45
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:38,200
Jesse became the father of King David.

46
00:02:38,670 --> 00:02:44,730
David the king became the father of
Solomon by her who had been Uriah’s wife.

47
00:02:46,150 --> 00:02:48,790
Solomon became the father of Rehoboam.

48
00:02:49,630 --> 00:02:51,850
Rehoboam became the father of Abijah.

49
00:02:53,050 --> 00:02:55,350
Abijah became the father of Asa.

50
00:02:55,810 --> 00:02:58,570
Asa became the father of Jehoshaphat.

51
00:02:58,610 --> 00:03:01,690
Jehoshaphat became the father of Joram.

52
00:03:02,270 --> 00:03:04,430
Joram became the father of Uzziah.

53
00:03:04,470 --> 00:03:07,850
Uzziah became the father of Jotham.

54
00:03:08,490 --> 00:03:11,370
Jotham became the father of Ahaz.

55
00:03:11,410 --> 00:03:14,290
Ahaz became the father of Hezekiah.

56
00:03:15,210 --> 00:03:18,150
Hezekiah became the father of Manasseh.

57
00:03:18,370 --> 00:03:20,960
Manasseh became the father of Amon.

58
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,670
Amon became the father of Josiah.

59
00:03:24,350 --> 00:03:30,790
Josiah became the father of Jechoniah and his
brothers at the time of the exile to Babylon.

60
00:03:31,790 --> 00:03:37,770
After the exile to Babylon, Jechoniah
became the father of Shealtiel.

61
00:03:37,810 --> 00:03:41,020
Shealtiel became the father of Zerubbabel.

62
00:03:41,060 --> 00:03:43,950
Zerubbabel became the father of Abiud.

63
00:03:44,610 --> 00:03:47,520
Abiud became the father of Eliakim.

64
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:50,490
Eliakim became the father of Azor.

65
00:03:51,130 --> 00:03:53,530
Azor became the father of Zadok.

66
00:03:54,390 --> 00:03:57,090
Zadok became the father of Achim.

67
00:03:57,130 --> 00:04:00,050
Achim became the father of Eliud.

68
00:04:00,650 --> 00:04:03,300
Eliud became the father of Eleazar.

69
00:04:03,340 --> 00:04:06,250
Eleazar became the father of Matthan.

70
00:04:06,290 --> 00:04:08,670
Matthan became the father of Jacob.

71
00:04:09,530 --> 00:04:16,930
Jacob became the father of Joseph, the husband
of Mary, from whom was born Jesus, who

72
00:04:16,970 --> 00:04:17,870
is called Christ.

73
00:04:18,380 --> 00:04:25,590
So all the generations from Abraham to
David are fourteen generations; from

74
00:04:25,630 --> 00:04:32,310
David to the exile to Babylon fourteen
generations; and from the carrying away to Babylon

75
00:04:32,350 --> 00:04:35,450
to the Christ, fourteen generations.

76
00:04:36,650 --> 00:04:43,190
Now the birth of Jesus Christ was like
this: After his mother, Mary, was engaged

77
00:04:43,230 --> 00:04:49,190
to Joseph, before they came together, she
was found pregnant by the Holy Spirit.

78
00:04:49,810 --> 00:04:56,030
Joseph, her husband, being a righteous man, and
not willing to make her a public example,

79
00:04:56,810 --> 00:04:58,590
intended to put her away secretly.

80
00:04:59,390 --> 00:05:05,410
But when he thought about these things, behold,
an angel of the Lord appeared to him

81
00:05:05,450 --> 00:05:12,390
in a dream, saying, “Joseph, son of David,
don’t be afraid to take to yourself Mary

82
00:05:12,430 --> 00:05:17,550
as your wife, for that which is conceived
in her is of the Holy Spirit.

83
00:05:17,916 --> 00:05:19,836
She shall give birth to a son.

84
00:05:21,016 --> 00:05:26,696
You shall name him Jesus, for it is he who
shall save his people from their sins.”

85
00:05:27,736 --> 00:05:33,596
Now all this has happened that it might
be fulfilled which was spoken by the Lord through

86
00:05:33,636 --> 00:05:40,196
the prophet, saying, “Behold, the virgin shall
be with child, and shall give birth to

87
00:05:40,236 --> 00:05:41,136
a son.

88
00:05:41,256 --> 00:05:47,796
They shall call his name Immanuel,” which
is, being interpreted, “God with us.”

89
00:05:49,036 --> 00:05:55,476
Joseph arose from his sleep, and did as
the angel of the Lord commanded him, and took

90
00:05:55,516 --> 00:06:01,716
his wife to himself; and didn’t know her
sexually until she had given birth to her firstborn

91
00:06:01,756 --> 00:06:02,656
son.

92
00:06:02,796 --> 00:06:04,176
He named him Jesus.

93
00:06:04,996 --> 00:06:06,916
Matthew, chapter two.

94
00:06:06,956 --> 00:06:14,016
Now when Jesus was born in Bethlehem of
Judea in the days of King Herod, behold, wise

95
00:06:14,056 --> 00:06:20,236
men from the east came to Jerusalem, saying, “Where
is he who is born King of the Jews?

96
00:06:21,136 --> 00:06:24,916
For we saw his star in the east, and have
come to worship him.”

97
00:06:25,576 --> 00:06:30,496
When King Herod heard it, he was troubled,
and all Jerusalem with him.

98
00:06:31,356 --> 00:06:37,036
Gathering together all the chief priests and
scribes of the people, he asked them where

99
00:06:37,076 --> 00:06:38,396
the Christ would be born.

100
00:06:39,036 --> 00:06:45,576
They said to him, “In Bethlehem of Judea,
for this is written through the prophet, ‘You

101
00:06:45,616 --> 00:06:52,276
Bethlehem, land of Judah, are in no way
least amongst the princes of Judah; for out

102
00:06:52,316 --> 00:06:57,916
of you shall come a governor who
shall shepherd my people, Israel.’” Then Herod secretly

103
00:06:57,956 --> 00:07:03,396
called the wise men, and learnt from them
exactly what time the star appeared.

104
00:07:04,576 --> 00:07:10,376
He sent them to Bethlehem, and said, “Go
and search diligently for the young child.

105
00:07:11,296 --> 00:07:16,576
When you have found him, bring me word, so
that I also may come and worship him.”

106
00:07:17,136 --> 00:07:23,396
They, having heard the king, went their way;
and behold, the star, which they saw in

107
00:07:23,436 --> 00:07:28,736
the east, went before them until it came
and stood over where the young child was.

108
00:07:29,776 --> 00:07:33,916
When they saw the star, they rejoiced with
exceedingly great joy.

109
00:07:34,736 --> 00:07:40,656
They came into the house and saw the young
child with Mary, his mother, and they fell

110
00:07:40,696 --> 00:07:42,076
down and worshipped him.

111
00:07:42,404 --> 00:07:49,004
Opening their treasures, they offered to
him gifts: gold, frankincense, and

112
00:07:49,044 --> 00:07:49,944
myrrh.

113
00:07:50,324 --> 00:07:56,684
Being warned in a dream not to return to
Herod, they went back to their own country another

114
00:07:56,724 --> 00:07:57,624
way.

115
00:07:57,684 --> 00:08:03,964
Now when they had departed, behold, an angel
of the Lord appeared to Joseph in a dream,

116
00:08:04,444 --> 00:08:11,424
saying, “Arise and take the young child
and his mother, and flee into Egypt, and

117
00:08:11,464 --> 00:08:16,984
stay there until I tell you, for Herod
will seek the young child to destroy him.”

118
00:08:17,624 --> 00:08:24,044
He arose and took the young child and
his mother by night and departed into Egypt, and

119
00:08:24,084 --> 00:08:29,644
was there until the death of Herod, that
it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the

120
00:08:29,684 --> 00:08:34,564
Lord through the prophet, saying, “Out of
Egypt I called my son.”

121
00:08:34,784 --> 00:08:41,784
Then Herod, when he saw that he was
mocked by the wise men, was exceedingly angry, and

122
00:08:41,824 --> 00:08:47,565
sent out and killed all the male children
who were in Bethlehem and in all the surrounding

123
00:08:47,604 --> 00:08:53,864
countryside, from two years old and under, according
to the exact time which he had learnt

124
00:08:53,904 --> 00:08:54,984
from the wise men.

125
00:08:55,484 --> 00:09:01,945
Then that which was spoken by Jeremiah
the prophet was fulfilled, saying, “A voice was

126
00:09:01,984 --> 00:09:08,784
heard in Ramah, lamentation, weeping and
great mourning, Rachel weeping for

127
00:09:08,824 --> 00:09:12,984
her children; she wouldn’t be comforted,
because they are no more.”

128
00:09:13,544 --> 00:09:20,124
But when Herod was dead, behold, an angel of
the Lord appeared in a dream to Joseph in

129
00:09:20,164 --> 00:09:26,884
Egypt, saying, “Arise and take the young
child and his mother, and go into the land

130
00:09:26,924 --> 00:09:31,204
of Israel, for those who sought the young
child’s life are dead.”

131
00:09:31,944 --> 00:09:36,904
He arose and took the young child and his
mother, and came into the land of Israel.

132
00:09:37,964 --> 00:09:42,784
But when he heard that Archelaus was reigning
over Judea in the place of his father,

133
00:09:42,824 --> 00:09:45,544
Herod, he was afraid to go there.

134
00:09:46,084 --> 00:09:52,364
Being warned in a dream, he withdrew into
the region of Galilee, and came and lived in

135
00:09:52,404 --> 00:09:57,925
a city called Nazareth; that it might
be fulfilled which was spoken through the prophets

136
00:09:57,964 --> 00:10:00,524
that he will be called a Nazarene.

137
00:10:01,524 --> 00:10:02,584
Matthew, chapter three.

138
00:10:03,521 --> 00:10:10,641
In those days, John the Baptiser came,
preaching in the wilderness of Judea, saying,

139
00:10:11,381 --> 00:10:14,381
“Repent, for the Kingdom of Heaven is at
hand!”

140
00:10:14,841 --> 00:10:21,761
For this is he who was spoken of by
Isaiah the prophet, saying, “The voice of one crying

141
00:10:21,801 --> 00:10:25,181
in the wilderness, make the way of the
Lord ready!

142
00:10:26,021 --> 00:10:27,301
Make his paths straight!”

143
00:10:28,361 --> 00:10:35,021
Now John himself wore clothing made of camel’s
hair with a leather belt around his waist.

144
00:10:36,081 --> 00:10:38,921
His food was locusts and wild honey.

145
00:10:40,061 --> 00:10:46,661
Then people from Jerusalem, all of Judea, and
all the region around the Jordan went out

146
00:10:46,701 --> 00:10:47,601
to him.

147
00:10:47,661 --> 00:10:51,581
They were baptised by him in the Jordan,
confessing their sins.

148
00:10:52,521 --> 00:10:58,961
But when he saw many of the Pharisees
and Sadducees coming for his baptism, he said to

149
00:10:59,001 --> 00:11:04,561
them, “You offspring of vipers, who warned
you to flee from the wrath to come?

150
00:11:05,541 --> 00:11:08,081
Therefore produce fruit worthy of
repentance!

151
00:11:09,041 --> 00:11:15,221
Don’t think to yourselves, ‘We have Abraham for
our father,’ for I tell you that God

152
00:11:15,261 --> 00:11:18,781
is able to raise up children to Abraham
from these stones.

153
00:11:20,001 --> 00:11:22,981
Even now the axe lies at the root of the
trees.

154
00:11:24,141 --> 00:11:29,821
Therefore every tree that doesn’t produce good fruit
is cut down, and cast into the fire.

155
00:11:30,501 --> 00:11:36,241
“I indeed baptise you in water for repentance,
but he who comes after me is mightier

156
00:11:36,281 --> 00:11:39,641
than I, whose sandals I am not worthy to
carry.

157
00:11:40,561 --> 00:11:42,721
He will baptise you in the Holy Spirit.

158
00:11:43,461 --> 00:11:48,701
His winnowing fork is in his hand,
and he will thoroughly cleanse his threshing floor.

159
00:11:49,421 --> 00:11:54,781
He will gather his wheat into the barn,
but the chaff he will burn up with unquenchable

160
00:11:54,821 --> 00:11:55,721
fire.”

161
00:11:56,261 --> 00:12:02,161
Then Jesus came from Galilee to the Jordan
to John, to be baptised by him.

162
00:12:03,101 --> 00:12:09,001
But John would have hindered him, saying, “I
need to be baptised by you, and you come

163
00:12:09,041 --> 00:12:09,421
to me?”

164
00:12:09,461 --> 00:12:15,941
But Jesus, answering, said to him, “Allow
it now, for this is the fitting

165
00:12:15,981 --> 00:12:18,321
way for us to fulfil all righteousness.”

166
00:12:19,481 --> 00:12:20,721
Then he allowed him.

167
00:12:21,601 --> 00:12:27,801
Jesus, when he was baptised, went up
directly from the water: and behold, the heavens

168
00:12:27,841 --> 00:12:28,941
were opened to him.

169
00:12:29,250 --> 00:12:33,930
He saw the Spirit of God descending as a
dove, and coming on him.

170
00:12:35,230 --> 00:12:41,830
Behold, a voice out of the heavens said,
“This is my beloved Son, with whom

171
00:12:41,870 --> 00:12:43,070
I am well pleased.”

172
00:12:44,250 --> 00:12:46,450
Matthew, chapter four.

173
00:12:46,490 --> 00:12:52,270
Then Jesus was led up by the Spirit into
the wilderness to be tempted by the devil.

174
00:12:53,070 --> 00:12:57,810
When he had fasted forty days and forty
nights, he was hungry afterward.

175
00:12:59,250 --> 00:13:05,410
The tempter came and said to him, “If you
are the Son of God, command that these stones

176
00:13:05,450 --> 00:13:06,450
become bread.”

177
00:13:07,050 --> 00:13:13,610
But he answered, “It is written, ‘Man
shall not live by bread alone, but by

178
00:13:13,650 --> 00:13:19,670
every word that proceeds out of God’s mouth.’”
Then the devil took him into the holy

179
00:13:19,710 --> 00:13:20,610
city.

180
00:13:20,850 --> 00:13:26,870
He set him on the pinnacle of the temple, and
said to him, “If you are the Son of God,

181
00:13:27,570 --> 00:13:33,610
throw yourself down, for it is written,
‘He will command his angels concerning you,’

182
00:13:34,390 --> 00:13:39,890
and, ‘On their hands they will bear you
up, so that you don’t dash your foot against

183
00:13:39,930 --> 00:13:46,630
a stone.’” Jesus said to him, “Again, it
is written, ‘You shall not test the

184
00:13:46,670 --> 00:13:53,790
Lord, your God.’” Again, the devil took
him to an exceedingly high mountain, and

185
00:13:53,830 --> 00:13:56,870
showed him all the kingdoms of the world
and their glory.

186
00:13:57,770 --> 00:14:03,710
He said to him, “I will give you all
of these things, if you will fall down and worship

187
00:14:03,750 --> 00:14:04,650
me.”

188
00:14:05,190 --> 00:14:08,730
Then Jesus said to him, “Get behind me,
Satan!

189
00:14:09,650 --> 00:14:15,050
For it is written, ‘You shall worship the
Lord your God, and you shall serve him only.’”

190
00:14:15,830 --> 00:14:20,630
Then the devil left him, and behold,
angels came and served him.

191
00:14:21,370 --> 00:14:27,070
Now when Jesus heard that John was
delivered up, he withdrew into Galilee.

192
00:14:27,250 --> 00:14:33,330
Leaving Nazareth, he came and lived in Capernaum,
which is by the sea, in the region

193
00:14:33,370 --> 00:14:39,070
of Zebulun and Naphtali, that it might
be fulfilled which was spoken through Isaiah the

194
00:14:39,110 --> 00:14:45,770
prophet, saying, “The land of Zebulun and
the land of Naphtali, towards the

195
00:14:45,810 --> 00:14:52,930
sea, beyond the Jordan, Galilee of the
Gentiles, the people who sat in darkness saw

196
00:14:52,970 --> 00:14:59,610
a great light; to those who sat in the
region and shadow of death, to them light has

197
00:14:59,650 --> 00:15:00,376
dawned.”

198
00:15:00,416 --> 00:15:05,736
From that time, Jesus began to preach, and
to say, “Repent!

199
00:15:06,456 --> 00:15:08,656
For the Kingdom of Heaven is at hand.”

200
00:15:09,656 --> 00:15:16,256
Walking by the sea of Galilee, he saw two
brothers: Simon, who is called Peter,

201
00:15:17,156 --> 00:15:22,516
and Andrew, his brother, casting a net
into the sea; for they were fishermen.

202
00:15:23,256 --> 00:15:28,176
He said to them, “Come after me, and I
will make you fishers for men.”

203
00:15:29,076 --> 00:15:32,256
They immediately left their nets and
followed him.

204
00:15:33,036 --> 00:15:39,636
Going on from there, he saw two other
brothers, James the son of Zebedee, and

205
00:15:39,676 --> 00:15:45,056
John his brother, in the boat with Zebedee
their father, mending their nets.

206
00:15:45,996 --> 00:15:46,896
He called them.

207
00:15:47,256 --> 00:15:51,216
They immediately left the boat and their
father, and followed him.

208
00:15:52,036 --> 00:15:58,136
Jesus went about in all Galilee, teaching
in their synagogues, preaching the Good News

209
00:15:58,176 --> 00:16:03,776
of the Kingdom, and healing every disease
and every sickness amongst the people.

210
00:16:04,256 --> 00:16:07,136
The report about him went out into all
Syria.

211
00:16:07,936 --> 00:16:13,396
They brought to him all who were
sick, afflicted with various diseases and torments,

212
00:16:14,436 --> 00:16:19,616
possessed with demons, epileptics, and
paralytics; and he healed them.

213
00:16:20,556 --> 00:16:27,256
Great multitudes from Galilee, Decapolis,
Jerusalem, Judea, and from beyond

214
00:16:27,296 --> 00:16:28,756
the Jordan followed him.

215
00:16:29,096 --> 00:16:31,296
Matthew, chapter five.

216
00:16:31,336 --> 00:16:34,516
Seeing the multitudes, he went up onto the
mountain.

217
00:16:35,456 --> 00:16:38,856
When he had sat down, his disciples came
to him.

218
00:16:39,496 --> 00:16:45,956
He opened his mouth and taught them, saying,
“Blessed are the poor in spirit, for theirs

219
00:16:45,996 --> 00:16:47,396
is the Kingdom of Heaven.

220
00:16:48,536 --> 00:16:51,756
Blessed are those who mourn, for they
shall be comforted.

221
00:16:52,196 --> 00:16:55,836
Blessed are the gentle, for they shall
inherit the earth.

222
00:16:56,776 --> 00:17:01,596
Blessed are those who hunger and thirst
for righteousness, for they shall be filled.

223
00:17:02,536 --> 00:17:05,636
Blessed are the merciful, for they shall
obtain mercy.

224
00:17:06,636 --> 00:17:09,816
Blessed are the pure in heart, for they
shall see God.

225
00:17:10,476 --> 00:17:14,396
Blessed are the peacemakers, for they
shall be called children of God.

226
00:17:15,336 --> 00:17:20,256
Blessed are those who have been persecuted
for righteousness’ sake, for theirs is the

227
00:17:20,296 --> 00:17:21,196
Kingdom of Heaven.

228
00:17:21,494 --> 00:17:28,274
“Blessed are you when people reproach you, persecute
you, and say all kinds of evil against

229
00:17:28,314 --> 00:17:30,594
you falsely, for my sake.

230
00:17:31,714 --> 00:17:36,934
Rejoice, and be exceedingly glad, for
great is your reward in heaven.

231
00:17:38,014 --> 00:17:41,494
For that is how they persecuted the
prophets who were before you.

232
00:17:42,014 --> 00:17:47,994
“You are the salt of the earth, but if the
salt has lost its flavour, with what will

233
00:17:48,034 --> 00:17:48,934
it be salted?

234
00:17:49,474 --> 00:17:55,594
It is then good for nothing, but to be
cast out and trodden under the feet of men.

235
00:17:56,494 --> 00:17:57,934
You are the light of the world.

236
00:17:58,354 --> 00:18:00,954
A city located on a hill can’t be hidden.

237
00:18:01,574 --> 00:18:07,314
Neither do you light a lamp and put it
under a measuring basket, but on a stand; and

238
00:18:07,354 --> 00:18:09,434
it shines to all who are in the house.

239
00:18:10,314 --> 00:18:17,394
Even so, let your light shine before men,
that they may see your good works and glorify

240
00:18:17,434 --> 00:18:18,914
your Father who is in heaven.

241
00:18:19,654 --> 00:18:23,134
“Don’t think that I came to destroy the
law or the prophets.

242
00:18:24,234 --> 00:18:27,734
I didn’t come to destroy, but to fulfil.

243
00:18:27,774 --> 00:18:34,314
For most certainly, I tell you, until heaven
and earth pass away, not even one smallest

244
00:18:34,354 --> 00:18:41,054
letter or one tiny pen stroke shall in any
way pass away from the law, until

245
00:18:41,094 --> 00:18:42,394
all things are accomplished.

246
00:18:43,294 --> 00:18:48,854
Therefore, whoever shall break one of these
least commandments and teach others to do

247
00:18:48,894 --> 00:18:55,594
so, shall be called least in the Kingdom
of Heaven; but whoever shall do and teach

248
00:18:55,634 --> 00:18:58,714
them shall be called great in the Kingdom
of Heaven.

249
00:18:59,374 --> 00:19:04,874
For I tell you that unless your
righteousness exceeds that of the scribes and Pharisees,

250
00:19:05,374 --> 00:19:08,754
there is no way you will enter into the
Kingdom of Heaven.

251
00:19:09,154 --> 00:19:14,674
“You have heard that it was said to
the ancient ones, ‘You shall not murder;’ and ‘Whoever

252
00:19:14,714 --> 00:19:17,714
murders will be in danger of the
judgement.’

253
00:19:17,754 --> 00:19:23,514
But I tell you that everyone who is angry
with his brother without a cause will be in

254
00:19:23,554 --> 00:19:25,554
danger of the judgement.

255
00:19:25,594 --> 00:19:28,794
Whoever says to his brother, ‘Raca!’

256
00:19:28,834 --> 00:19:30,714
will be in danger of the council.

257
00:19:31,794 --> 00:19:33,574
Whoever says, ‘You fool!’

258
00:19:33,614 --> 00:19:36,934
will be in danger of the fire of Gehenna.

259
00:19:37,109 --> 00:19:42,609
“If therefore you are offering your gift at
the altar, and there remember that your brother

260
00:19:42,649 --> 00:19:48,749
has anything against you, leave your gift
there before the altar, and go your way.

261
00:19:49,909 --> 00:19:54,849
First be reconciled to your brother, and
then come and offer your gift.

262
00:19:55,449 --> 00:20:01,169
Agree with your adversary quickly while you are
with him on the way; lest perhaps the

263
00:20:01,209 --> 00:20:07,249
prosecutor deliver you to the judge, and the
judge deliver you to the officer, and you

264
00:20:07,289 --> 00:20:08,609
be cast into prison.

265
00:20:08,969 --> 00:20:14,389
Most certainly I tell you, you shall by no
means get out of there until you have paid

266
00:20:14,429 --> 00:20:15,369
the last penny.

267
00:20:15,989 --> 00:20:21,229
“You have heard that it was said, ‘You
shall not commit adultery;’ but I tell you that

268
00:20:21,269 --> 00:20:26,989
everyone who gazes at a woman to lust
after her has committed adultery with her already

269
00:20:27,029 --> 00:20:27,929
in his heart.

270
00:20:28,749 --> 00:20:33,949
If your right eye causes you to stumble,
pluck it out and throw it away from you.

271
00:20:34,389 --> 00:20:39,709
For it is more profitable for you that
one of your members should perish than for your

272
00:20:39,749 --> 00:20:42,069
whole body to be cast into Gehenna.

273
00:20:42,929 --> 00:20:48,309
If your right hand causes you to stumble,
cut it off, and throw it away from you.

274
00:20:48,689 --> 00:20:53,829
For it is more profitable for you that
one of your members should perish, than for your

275
00:20:53,869 --> 00:20:56,109
whole body to be cast into Gehenna.

276
00:20:56,609 --> 00:21:02,869
“It was also said, ‘Whoever shall put away his
wife, let him give her a writing of divorce,’

277
00:21:03,949 --> 00:21:09,809
but I tell you that whoever puts away
his wife, except for the cause of sexual immorality,

278
00:21:10,349 --> 00:21:15,809
makes her an adulteress; and whoever marries
her when she is put away commits adultery.

279
00:21:16,649 --> 00:21:21,609
“Again you have heard that it was said
to the ancient ones, ‘You shall not make false

280
00:21:21,649 --> 00:21:28,769
vows, but shall perform to the Lord your vows,’
but I tell you, don’t swear at all: neither

281
00:21:28,809 --> 00:21:34,789
by heaven, for it is the throne of God;
nor by the earth, for it is the footstool of

282
00:21:34,829 --> 00:21:39,849
his feet; nor by Jerusalem, for it is the
city of the great King.

283
00:21:41,009 --> 00:21:46,109
Neither shall you swear by your head, for
you can’t make one hair white or black.

284
00:21:47,269 --> 00:21:50,649
But let your ‘Yes’ be ‘Yes’ and your ‘No’
be ‘No.’

285
00:21:51,005 --> 00:21:54,345
Whatever is more than these is of the evil
one.

286
00:21:55,345 --> 00:22:00,825
“You have heard that it was said, ‘An eye
for an eye, and a tooth for a tooth.’

287
00:22:01,765 --> 00:22:08,485
But I tell you, don’t resist him who is
evil; but whoever strikes you on your right cheek,

288
00:22:09,105 --> 00:22:10,605
turn to him the other also.

289
00:22:11,525 --> 00:22:16,525
If anyone sues you to take away your coat,
let him have your cloak also.

290
00:22:17,465 --> 00:22:22,305
Whoever compels you to go one mile, go
with him two.

291
00:22:22,345 --> 00:22:28,085
Give to him who asks you, and don’t turn
away him who desires to borrow from you.

292
00:22:28,485 --> 00:22:33,065
“You have heard that it was said, ‘You
shall love your neighbour and hate your enemy.’

293
00:22:33,685 --> 00:22:40,105
But I tell you, love your enemies, bless those
who curse you, do good to those who hate

294
00:22:40,145 --> 00:22:46,085
you, and pray for those who mistreat you
and persecute you, that you may be children

295
00:22:46,125 --> 00:22:48,105
of your Father who is in heaven.

296
00:22:48,745 --> 00:22:54,965
For he makes his sun to rise on the evil
and the good, and sends rain on the just and

297
00:22:55,005 --> 00:22:55,905
the unjust.

298
00:22:56,825 --> 00:23:01,165
For if you love those who love you, what
reward do you have?

299
00:23:02,025 --> 00:23:04,585
Don’t even the tax collectors do the same?

300
00:23:05,085 --> 00:23:08,945
If you only greet your friends, what more
do you do than others?

301
00:23:09,625 --> 00:23:12,085
Don’t even the tax collectors do the same?

302
00:23:12,985 --> 00:23:17,825
Therefore you shall be perfect, just as
your Father in heaven is perfect.

303
00:23:18,485 --> 00:23:21,165
Matthew, chapter six.

304
00:23:21,205 --> 00:23:26,805
“Be careful that you don’t do your charitable
giving before men, to be seen by them,

305
00:23:27,585 --> 00:23:30,765
or else you have no reward from your
Father who is in heaven.

306
00:23:31,445 --> 00:23:37,925
Therefore, when you do merciful deeds,
don’t sound a trumpet before yourself, as

307
00:23:37,965 --> 00:23:43,155
the hypocrites do in the synagogues and in
the streets, that they may get glory from

308
00:23:43,195 --> 00:23:44,095
men.

309
00:23:44,415 --> 00:23:48,495
Most certainly I tell you, they have
received their reward.

310
00:23:49,235 --> 00:23:54,875
But when you do merciful deeds, don’t let
your left hand know what your right hand does,

311
00:23:55,335 --> 00:24:01,215
so that your merciful deeds may be in
secret, then your Father who sees in secret will

312
00:24:01,255 --> 00:24:02,295
reward you openly.

313
00:24:02,935 --> 00:24:08,715
“When you pray, you shall not be as the
hypocrites, for they love to stand and pray in

314
00:24:08,755 --> 00:24:13,915
the synagogues and in the corners of the
streets, that they may be seen by men.

315
00:24:14,271 --> 00:24:18,211
Most certainly, I tell you, they have
received their reward.

316
00:24:19,451 --> 00:24:26,871
But you, when you pray, enter into your
inner room, and having shut your door, pray

317
00:24:26,911 --> 00:24:33,271
to your Father who is in secret; and your
Father who sees in secret will reward you openly.

318
00:24:33,311 --> 00:24:39,811
In praying, don’t use vain repetitions as
the Gentiles do; for they think that they

319
00:24:39,851 --> 00:24:41,611
will be heard for their much speaking.

320
00:24:42,491 --> 00:24:48,531
Therefore don’t be like them, for your Father
knows what things you need before you ask

321
00:24:48,571 --> 00:24:49,471
him.

322
00:24:49,771 --> 00:24:55,211
Pray like this: “‘Our Father in heaven,
may your name be kept holy.

323
00:24:56,271 --> 00:24:57,351
Let your Kingdom come.

324
00:24:57,971 --> 00:25:01,071
Let your will be done on earth as it is in
heaven.

325
00:25:02,091 --> 00:25:04,151
Give us today our daily bread.

326
00:25:04,911 --> 00:25:08,751
Forgive us our debts, as we also forgive
our debtors.

327
00:25:08,791 --> 00:25:14,031
Bring us not into temptation, but deliver
us from the evil one.

328
00:25:14,411 --> 00:25:18,411
For yours is the Kingdom, the power, and
the glory forever.

329
00:25:19,511 --> 00:25:20,411
Amen.’

330
00:25:20,751 --> 00:25:26,151
“For if you forgive men their trespasses,
your heavenly Father will also forgive you.

331
00:25:26,991 --> 00:25:32,111
But if you don’t forgive men their
trespasses, neither will your Father forgive your

332
00:25:32,151 --> 00:25:33,051
trespasses.

333
00:25:33,551 --> 00:25:38,811
“Moreover when you fast, don’t be like the
hypocrites, with sad faces.

334
00:25:39,451 --> 00:25:44,051
For they disfigure their faces that they
may be seen by men to be fasting.

335
00:25:44,971 --> 00:25:48,691
Most certainly I tell you, they have
received their reward.

336
00:25:49,491 --> 00:25:55,731
But you, when you fast, anoint your head and
wash your face, so that you are not seen

337
00:25:55,771 --> 00:26:01,771
by men to be fasting, but by your Father
who is in secret; and your Father, who sees

338
00:26:01,811 --> 00:26:03,731
in secret, will reward you.

339
00:26:04,811 --> 00:26:11,131
“Don’t lay up treasures for yourselves on
the earth, where moth and rust consume, and

340
00:26:11,171 --> 00:26:16,371
where thieves break through and steal; but
lay up for yourselves treasures in heaven,

341
00:26:17,271 --> 00:26:22,331
where neither moth nor rust consume, and
where thieves don’t break through and steal;

342
00:26:22,371 --> 00:26:26,851
for where your treasure is, there your
heart will be also.

343
00:26:27,911 --> 00:26:29,971
“The lamp of the body is the eye.

344
00:26:30,571 --> 00:26:35,151
If therefore your eye is sound, your whole
body will be full of light.

345
00:26:36,231 --> 00:26:40,331
But if your eye is evil, your whole body
will be full of darkness.

346
00:26:40,947 --> 00:26:46,047
If therefore the light that is in you is
darkness, how great is the darkness!

347
00:26:47,087 --> 00:26:53,627
“No one can serve two masters, for either he
will hate the one and love the other, or

348
00:26:53,667 --> 00:26:56,987
else he will be devoted to one and despise
the other.

349
00:26:57,627 --> 00:27:00,327
You can’t serve both God and Mammon.

350
00:27:00,767 --> 00:27:07,087
Therefore I tell you, don’t be anxious for
your life: what you will eat, or what you

351
00:27:07,127 --> 00:27:10,987
will drink; nor yet for your body, what
you will wear.

352
00:27:11,887 --> 00:27:15,767
Isn’t life more than food, and the body
more than clothing?

353
00:27:15,807 --> 00:27:22,287
See the birds of the sky, that they don’t
sow, neither do they reap, nor gather

354
00:27:22,327 --> 00:27:23,407
into barns.

355
00:27:23,867 --> 00:27:25,607
Your heavenly Father feeds them.

356
00:27:26,187 --> 00:27:28,607
Aren’t you of much more value than they?

357
00:27:29,327 --> 00:27:33,967
“Which of you by being anxious, can add
one moment to his lifespan?

358
00:27:34,887 --> 00:27:37,167
Why are you anxious about clothing?

359
00:27:37,967 --> 00:27:40,827
Consider the lilies of the field, how they
grow.

360
00:27:41,487 --> 00:27:48,187
They don’t toil, neither do they spin, yet I
tell you that even Solomon in all his glory

361
00:27:48,227 --> 00:27:50,467
was not dressed like one of these.

362
00:27:51,027 --> 00:27:56,887
But if God so clothes the grass of
the field, which today exists and tomorrow is thrown

363
00:27:56,927 --> 00:28:02,047
into the oven, won’t he much more clothe
you, you of little faith?

364
00:28:02,667 --> 00:28:08,147
“Therefore don’t be anxious, saying, ‘What
will we eat?’, ‘What will we drink?’

365
00:28:08,427 --> 00:28:10,567
or, ‘With what will we be clothed?’

366
00:28:11,627 --> 00:28:17,727
For the Gentiles seek after all these
things; for your heavenly Father knows that you

367
00:28:17,767 --> 00:28:18,947
need all these things.

368
00:28:19,507 --> 00:28:25,187
But seek first God’s Kingdom and his
righteousness; and all these things will be given

369
00:28:25,227 --> 00:28:26,167
to you as well.

370
00:28:26,987 --> 00:28:32,467
Therefore don’t be anxious for tomorrow,
for tomorrow will be anxious for itself.

371
00:28:33,687 --> 00:28:35,867
Each day’s own evil is sufficient.

372
00:28:37,187 --> 00:28:39,467
Matthew, chapter seven.

373
00:28:39,507 --> 00:28:42,407
“Don’t judge, so that you won’t be judged.

374
00:28:43,147 --> 00:28:48,507
For with whatever judgement you judge, you
will be judged; and with whatever measure

375
00:28:48,547 --> 00:28:51,427
you measure, it will be measured to you.

376
00:28:52,267 --> 00:28:57,907
Why do you see the speck that is in
your brother’s eye, but don’t consider the beam that

377
00:28:57,947 --> 00:28:58,907
is in your own eye?

378
00:28:59,141 --> 00:29:05,361
Or how will you tell your brother, ‘Let
me remove the speck from your eye,’ and behold,

379
00:29:06,001 --> 00:29:07,441
the beam is in your own eye?

380
00:29:08,461 --> 00:29:09,461
You hypocrite!

381
00:29:10,261 --> 00:29:16,201
First remove the beam out of your own eye,
and then you can see clearly to remove the

382
00:29:16,241 --> 00:29:17,961
speck out of your brother’s eye.

383
00:29:18,481 --> 00:29:23,981
“Don’t give that which is holy to the
dogs, neither throw your pearls before the pigs,

384
00:29:24,621 --> 00:29:29,581
lest perhaps they trample them under their
feet, and turn and tear you to pieces.

385
00:29:30,821 --> 00:29:33,201
“Ask, and it will be given you.

386
00:29:33,861 --> 00:29:35,721
Seek, and you will find.

387
00:29:36,421 --> 00:29:38,761
Knock, and it will be opened for you.

388
00:29:39,261 --> 00:29:41,161
For everyone who asks receives.

389
00:29:42,261 --> 00:29:43,481
He who seeks finds.

390
00:29:44,181 --> 00:29:46,581
To him who knocks it will be opened.

391
00:29:47,561 --> 00:29:53,521
Or who is there amongst you who, if his
son asks him for bread, will give him a stone?

392
00:29:54,001 --> 00:29:57,121
Or if he asks for a fish, who will give
him a serpent?

393
00:29:57,741 --> 00:30:04,361
If you then, being evil, know how to give
good gifts to your children, how much more

394
00:30:04,401 --> 00:30:08,761
will your Father who is in heaven give
good things to those who ask him!

395
00:30:09,181 --> 00:30:16,181
Therefore, whatever you desire for men to
do to you, you shall also do to them; for

396
00:30:16,221 --> 00:30:18,021
this is the law and the prophets.

397
00:30:18,701 --> 00:30:25,301
“Enter in by the narrow gate; for the gate
is wide and the way is broad that leads to

398
00:30:25,341 --> 00:30:28,881
destruction, and there are many who enter
in by it.

399
00:30:29,721 --> 00:30:33,981
How narrow is the gate and the way is
restricted that leads to life!

400
00:30:34,881 --> 00:30:36,381
There are few who find it.

401
00:30:36,901 --> 00:30:43,141
“Beware of false prophets, who come to
you in sheep’s clothing, but inwardly are ravening

402
00:30:43,181 --> 00:30:44,081
wolves.

403
00:30:44,421 --> 00:30:46,121
By their fruits you will know them.

404
00:30:46,941 --> 00:30:51,101
Do you gather grapes from thorns or figs
from thistles?

405
00:30:51,521 --> 00:30:58,421
Even so, every good tree produces good
fruit, but the corrupt tree produces evil fruit.

406
00:30:59,041 --> 00:31:04,561
A good tree can’t produce evil fruit,
neither can a corrupt tree produce good fruit.

407
00:31:05,281 --> 00:31:10,701
Every tree that doesn’t grow good fruit is
cut down and thrown into the fire.

408
00:31:11,641 --> 00:31:13,981
Therefore by their fruits you will know
them.

409
00:31:14,581 --> 00:31:21,721
“Not everyone who says to me, ‘Lord, Lord,’
will enter into the Kingdom of Heaven, but

410
00:31:21,761 --> 00:31:24,801
he who does the will of my Father who is
in heaven.

411
00:31:25,042 --> 00:31:31,762
Many will tell me in that day, ‘Lord,
Lord, didn’t we prophesy in your name,

412
00:31:32,622 --> 00:31:37,262
in your name cast out demons, and in your
name do many mighty works?’

413
00:31:38,102 --> 00:31:41,162
Then I will tell them, ‘I never knew you.

414
00:31:41,842 --> 00:31:44,722
Depart from me, you who work iniquity.’

415
00:31:45,382 --> 00:31:50,882
“Everyone therefore who hears these words
of mine and does them, I will liken him to

416
00:31:50,922 --> 00:31:53,722
a wise man who built his house on a rock.

417
00:31:54,382 --> 00:32:01,302
The rain came down, the floods came, and
the winds blew and beat on that house; and

418
00:32:01,342 --> 00:32:04,342
it didn’t fall, for it was founded on the
rock.

419
00:32:04,942 --> 00:32:10,402
Everyone who hears these words of mine and
doesn’t do them will be like a foolish man

420
00:32:10,442 --> 00:32:12,342
who built his house on the sand.

421
00:32:13,322 --> 00:32:19,682
The rain came down, the floods came, and the
winds blew and beat on that house; and it

422
00:32:19,722 --> 00:32:21,882
fell—and its fall was great.”

423
00:32:22,462 --> 00:32:28,302
When Jesus had finished saying these things,
the multitudes were astonished at his teaching,

424
00:32:29,222 --> 00:32:32,902
for he taught them with authority, and not
like the scribes.

425
00:32:33,762 --> 00:32:35,722
Matthew, chapter eight.

426
00:32:35,762 --> 00:32:40,542
When he came down from the mountain, great
multitudes followed him.

427
00:32:41,102 --> 00:32:47,802
Behold, a leper came to him and worshipped
him, saying, “Lord, if you want to,

428
00:32:48,262 --> 00:32:49,362
you can make me clean.”

429
00:32:50,562 --> 00:32:55,062
Jesus stretched out his hand and touched
him, saying, “I want to.

430
00:32:55,622 --> 00:32:56,522
Be made clean.”

431
00:32:57,342 --> 00:33:00,082
Immediately his leprosy was cleansed.

432
00:33:00,262 --> 00:33:07,422
Jesus said to him, “See that you tell
nobody; but go, show yourself to the priest, and

433
00:33:07,462 --> 00:33:11,882
offer the gift that Moses commanded, as a
testimony to them.”

434
00:33:12,362 --> 00:33:19,202
When he came into Capernaum, a centurion came
to him, asking him for help, saying, “Lord,

435
00:33:19,822 --> 00:33:24,222
my servant lies in the house paralysed,
grievously tormented.”

436
00:33:24,982 --> 00:33:27,942
Jesus said to him, “I will come and heal
him.”

437
00:33:28,802 --> 00:33:34,242
The centurion answered, “Lord, I’m not
worthy for you to come under my roof.

438
00:33:34,922 --> 00:33:38,242
Just say the word, and my servant will be
healed.

439
00:33:39,062 --> 00:33:43,542
For I am also a man under authority,
having under myself soldiers.

440
00:33:44,542 --> 00:33:51,102
I tell this one, ‘Go,’ and he goes; and
tell another, ‘Come,’ and he comes;

441
00:33:51,142 --> 00:33:55,422
and tell my servant, ‘Do this,’ and he
does it.”

442
00:33:55,666 --> 00:34:02,166
When Jesus heard it, he marvelled and said
to those who followed, “Most certainly

443
00:34:02,206 --> 00:34:07,766
I tell you, I haven’t found so great a
faith, not even in Israel.

444
00:34:08,426 --> 00:34:14,046
I tell you that many will come from the
east and the west, and will sit down with Abraham,

445
00:34:14,806 --> 00:34:20,126
Isaac, and Jacob in the Kingdom of Heaven,
but the children of the Kingdom will be thrown

446
00:34:20,166 --> 00:34:21,766
out into the outer darkness.

447
00:34:22,686 --> 00:34:24,905
There will be weeping and gnashing of
teeth.”

448
00:34:25,606 --> 00:34:29,006
Jesus said to the centurion, “Go your way.

449
00:34:29,606 --> 00:34:32,146
Let it be done for you as you have
believed.”

450
00:34:33,186 --> 00:34:35,326
His servant was healed in that hour.

451
00:34:35,726 --> 00:34:41,385
When Jesus came into Peter’s house, he saw
his wife’s mother lying sick with a fever.

452
00:34:42,226 --> 00:34:45,266
He touched her hand, and the fever left
her.

453
00:34:45,966 --> 00:34:47,826
So she got up and served him.

454
00:34:48,426 --> 00:34:52,346
When evening came, they brought to him
many possessed with demons.

455
00:34:53,686 --> 00:35:00,286
He cast out the spirits with a word, and
healed all who were sick, that it might be fulfilled

456
00:35:00,326 --> 00:35:06,866
which was spoken through Isaiah the
prophet, saying, “He took our infirmities and

457
00:35:06,906 --> 00:35:07,806
bore our diseases.”

458
00:35:08,646 --> 00:35:14,866
Now when Jesus saw great multitudes around him,
he gave the order to depart to the other

459
00:35:14,906 --> 00:35:15,806
side.

460
00:35:16,706 --> 00:35:22,346
A scribe came and said to him, “Teacher, I
will follow you wherever you go.”

461
00:35:22,926 --> 00:35:30,166
Jesus said to him, “The foxes have holes
and the birds of the sky have nests, but

462
00:35:30,206 --> 00:35:33,226
the Son of Man has nowhere to lay his
head.”

463
00:35:34,246 --> 00:35:40,826
Another of his disciples said to him,
“Lord, allow me first to go and bury my

464
00:35:40,866 --> 00:35:41,766
father.”

465
00:35:41,926 --> 00:35:47,806
But Jesus said to him, “Follow me, and
leave the dead to bury their own dead.”

466
00:35:48,766 --> 00:35:52,366
When he got into a boat, his disciples
followed him.

467
00:35:53,266 --> 00:35:59,766
Behold, a violent storm came up on the
sea, so much that the boat was covered with

468
00:35:59,806 --> 00:36:01,906
the waves; but he was asleep.

469
00:36:02,686 --> 00:36:07,606
The disciples came to him and woke him up,
saying, “Save us, Lord!

470
00:36:08,066 --> 00:36:08,986
We are dying!”

471
00:36:09,986 --> 00:36:14,706
He said to them, “Why are you fearful, O
you of little faith?”

472
00:36:15,706 --> 00:36:21,026
Then he got up, rebuked the wind and the
sea, and there was a great calm.

473
00:36:21,066 --> 00:36:27,746
The men marvelled, saying, “What kind of
man is this, that even the wind and

474
00:36:27,786 --> 00:36:29,006
the sea obey him?”

475
00:36:29,245 --> 00:36:35,805
When he came to the other side, into
the country of the Gergesenes, two people possessed

476
00:36:35,845 --> 00:36:42,385
by demons met him there, coming out of the
tombs, exceedingly fierce, so that

477
00:36:42,425 --> 00:36:44,085
nobody could pass that way.

478
00:36:45,085 --> 00:36:51,385
Behold, they cried out, saying, “What do
we have to do with you, Jesus, Son of God?

479
00:36:52,145 --> 00:36:54,905
Have you come here to torment us before
the time?”

480
00:36:55,925 --> 00:36:59,925
Now there was a herd of many pigs feeding
far away from them.

481
00:37:00,825 --> 00:37:06,985
The demons begged him, saying, “If you cast us
out, permit us to go away into the herd

482
00:37:07,025 --> 00:37:07,925
of pigs.”

483
00:37:08,305 --> 00:37:09,825
He said to them, “Go!”

484
00:37:10,665 --> 00:37:16,465
They came out and went into the herd of
pigs; and behold, the whole herd of pigs rushed

485
00:37:16,505 --> 00:37:20,005
down the cliff into the sea and died in
the water.

486
00:37:21,005 --> 00:37:27,505
Those who fed them fled and went away
into the city and told everything, including what

487
00:37:27,545 --> 00:37:29,825
happened to those who were possessed with
demons.

488
00:37:30,805 --> 00:37:33,985
Behold, all the city came out to meet
Jesus.

489
00:37:34,805 --> 00:37:38,665
When they saw him, they begged that he
would depart from their borders.

490
00:37:39,805 --> 00:37:42,685
Matthew, chapter nine.

491
00:37:42,725 --> 00:37:47,065
He entered into a boat and crossed over,
and came into his own city.

492
00:37:48,005 --> 00:37:52,825
Behold, they brought to him a man who was
paralysed, lying on a bed.

493
00:37:53,505 --> 00:37:59,045
Jesus, seeing their faith, said to the
paralytic, “Son, cheer up!

494
00:37:59,465 --> 00:38:01,005
Your sins are forgiven you.”

495
00:38:02,045 --> 00:38:07,165
Behold, some of the scribes said to
themselves, “This man blasphemes.”

496
00:38:07,365 --> 00:38:12,245
Jesus, knowing their thoughts, said, “Why
do you think evil in your hearts?

497
00:38:12,845 --> 00:38:19,385
For which is easier, to say, ‘Your sins
are forgiven;’ or to say, ‘Get up,

498
00:38:19,425 --> 00:38:20,325
and walk?’

499
00:38:21,145 --> 00:38:26,955
But that you may know that the Son of
Man has authority on earth to forgive sins—” (then

500
00:38:26,995 --> 00:38:32,525
he said to the paralytic), “Get up, and
take up your mat, and go to your house.”

501
00:38:33,585 --> 00:38:35,825
He arose and departed to his house.

502
00:38:36,445 --> 00:38:42,125
But when the multitudes saw it, they
marvelled and glorified God, who had given such

503
00:38:42,165 --> 00:38:43,285
authority to men.

504
00:38:44,445 --> 00:38:50,365
As Jesus passed by from there, he saw
a man called Matthew sitting at the tax collection

505
00:38:50,405 --> 00:38:51,305
office.

506
00:38:51,525 --> 00:38:53,505
He said to him, “Follow me.”

507
00:38:54,185 --> 00:38:56,125
He got up and followed him.

508
00:38:56,440 --> 00:39:03,040
As he sat in the house, behold, many tax
collectors and sinners came and sat down

509
00:39:03,080 --> 00:39:04,680
with Jesus and his disciples.

510
00:39:05,740 --> 00:39:12,340
When the Pharisees saw it, they said to
his disciples, “Why does your teacher eat with

511
00:39:12,380 --> 00:39:14,000
tax collectors and sinners?”

512
00:39:14,040 --> 00:39:20,360
When Jesus heard it, he said to them, “Those
who are healthy have no need for a physician,

513
00:39:21,120 --> 00:39:22,600
but those who are sick do.

514
00:39:23,500 --> 00:39:30,360
But you go and learn what this means: ‘I
desire mercy, and not sacrifice,’ for

515
00:39:30,400 --> 00:39:33,940
I came not to call the righteous, but
sinners to repentance.”

516
00:39:34,960 --> 00:39:41,460
Then John’s disciples came to him, saying, “Why
do we and the Pharisees fast often, but

517
00:39:41,500 --> 00:39:42,920
your disciples don’t fast?”

518
00:39:43,960 --> 00:39:49,520
Jesus said to them, “Can the friends of
the bridegroom mourn as long as the bridegroom

519
00:39:49,560 --> 00:39:50,460
is with them?

520
00:39:50,780 --> 00:39:56,200
But the days will come when the bridegroom
will be taken away from them, and then they

521
00:39:56,240 --> 00:39:57,140
will fast.

522
00:39:58,020 --> 00:40:04,260
No one puts a piece of unshrunk cloth on
an old garment; for the patch would tear away

523
00:40:04,300 --> 00:40:07,260
from the garment, and a worse hole is
made.

524
00:40:08,100 --> 00:40:14,440
Neither do people put new wine into old
wine skins, or else the skins would burst, and

525
00:40:14,480 --> 00:40:17,160
the wine be spilled, and the skins ruined.

526
00:40:18,040 --> 00:40:23,700
No, they put new wine into fresh wine
skins, and both are preserved.”

527
00:40:24,540 --> 00:40:29,980
While he told these things to them,
behold, a ruler came and worshipped him, saying,

528
00:40:31,060 --> 00:40:36,420
“My daughter has just died, but come and
lay your hand on her, and she will live.”

529
00:40:37,580 --> 00:40:41,320
Jesus got up and followed him, as did his
disciples.

530
00:40:42,120 --> 00:40:47,760
Behold, a woman who had a discharge of
blood for twelve years came behind him, and touched

531
00:40:47,800 --> 00:40:53,560
the fringe of his garment; for she said
within herself, “If I just touch his garment,

532
00:40:54,160 --> 00:40:55,240
I will be made well.”

533
00:40:56,260 --> 00:41:02,000
But Jesus, turning around and seeing her,
said, “Daughter, cheer up!

534
00:41:02,560 --> 00:41:04,300
Your faith has made you well.”

535
00:41:05,220 --> 00:41:07,840
And the woman was made well from that
hour.

536
00:41:08,700 --> 00:41:14,760
When Jesus came into the ruler’s house and
saw the flute players and the crowd in noisy

537
00:41:14,800 --> 00:41:21,620
disorder, he said to them, “Make room,
because the girl isn’t dead, but sleeping.”

538
00:41:22,780 --> 00:41:24,180
They were ridiculing him.

539
00:41:24,450 --> 00:41:31,150
But when the crowd was sent out, he entered
in, took her by the hand, and the girl

540
00:41:31,190 --> 00:41:32,090
arose.

541
00:41:32,890 --> 00:41:36,110
The report of this went out into all that
land.

542
00:41:37,210 --> 00:41:43,750
As Jesus passed by from there, two blind
men followed him, calling out and saying,

543
00:41:44,750 --> 00:41:46,790
“Have mercy on us, son of David!”

544
00:41:47,370 --> 00:41:51,230
When he had come into the house, the blind
men came to him.

545
00:41:51,890 --> 00:41:56,670
Jesus said to them, “Do you believe that I
am able to do this?”

546
00:41:57,350 --> 00:41:59,610
They told him, “Yes, Lord.”

547
00:42:00,690 --> 00:42:05,990
Then he touched their eyes, saying, “According
to your faith be it done to you.”

548
00:42:06,870 --> 00:42:08,190
Then their eyes were opened.

549
00:42:09,030 --> 00:42:14,010
Jesus strictly commanded them, saying,
“See that no one knows about this.”

550
00:42:14,890 --> 00:42:19,110
But they went out and spread abroad his
fame in all that land.

551
00:42:19,850 --> 00:42:26,450
As they went out, behold, a mute man who
was demon possessed was brought to him.

552
00:42:26,890 --> 00:42:30,070
When the demon was cast out, the mute man
spoke.

553
00:42:30,750 --> 00:42:36,270
The multitudes marvelled, saying, “Nothing
like this has ever been seen in Israel!”

554
00:42:37,350 --> 00:42:42,970
But the Pharisees said, “By the prince of
the demons, he casts out demons.”

555
00:42:43,870 --> 00:42:50,070
Jesus went about all the cities and
the villages, teaching in their synagogues and preaching

556
00:42:50,110 --> 00:42:56,390
the Good News of the Kingdom, and
healing every disease and every sickness amongst the

557
00:42:56,430 --> 00:42:57,330
people.

558
00:42:57,390 --> 00:43:03,230
But when he saw the multitudes, he was
moved with compassion for them because they were

559
00:43:03,270 --> 00:43:06,770
harassed and scattered, like sheep without
a shepherd.

560
00:43:07,890 --> 00:43:14,450
Then he said to his disciples, “The
harvest indeed is plentiful, but the labourers are

561
00:43:14,490 --> 00:43:15,350
few.

562
00:43:15,390 --> 00:43:20,770
Pray therefore that the Lord of the
harvest will send out labourers into his harvest.”

563
00:43:22,170 --> 00:43:24,970
Matthew, chapter ten.

564
00:43:25,010 --> 00:43:31,050
He called to himself his twelve disciples,
and gave them authority over unclean spirits,

565
00:43:31,090 --> 00:43:35,990
to cast them out, and to heal every
disease and every sickness.

566
00:43:36,930 --> 00:43:39,390
Now the names of the twelve apostles are
these.

567
00:43:39,914 --> 00:43:47,134
The first, Simon, who is called Peter;
Andrew, his brother; James

568
00:43:47,494 --> 00:43:54,294
the son of Zebedee; John, his brother;
Philip; Bartholomew; Thomas;

569
00:43:55,774 --> 00:44:03,294
Matthew the tax collector; James the son
of Alphaeus; Lebbaeus, who was also called Thaddaeus;

570
00:44:03,334 --> 00:44:08,174
Simon the Zealot; and Judas Iscariot, who
also betrayed him.

571
00:44:08,214 --> 00:44:15,494
Jesus sent these twelve out and commanded
them, saying, “Don’t go amongst the Gentiles,

572
00:44:15,834 --> 00:44:18,774
and don’t enter into any city of the
Samaritans.

573
00:44:19,554 --> 00:44:23,114
Rather, go to the lost sheep of the house
of Israel.

574
00:44:24,114 --> 00:44:28,554
As you go, preach, saying, ‘The Kingdom of
Heaven is at hand!’

575
00:44:29,454 --> 00:44:32,954
Heal the sick, cleanse the lepers, and
cast out demons.

576
00:44:33,814 --> 00:44:36,674
Freely you received, so freely give.

577
00:44:37,274 --> 00:44:41,214
Don’t take any gold, silver, or brass in
your money belts.

578
00:44:41,994 --> 00:44:48,574
Take no bag for your journey, neither two
coats, nor sandals, nor staff: for the labourer

579
00:44:48,614 --> 00:44:50,134
is worthy of his food.

580
00:44:50,814 --> 00:44:57,354
Into whatever city or village you enter, find
out who in it is worthy, and stay there

581
00:44:57,394 --> 00:44:58,474
until you go on.

582
00:44:59,614 --> 00:45:02,314
As you enter into the household, greet it.

583
00:45:03,194 --> 00:45:09,374
If the household is worthy, let your peace come
on it, but if it isn’t worthy, let your

584
00:45:09,414 --> 00:45:10,674
peace return to you.

585
00:45:11,254 --> 00:45:17,694
Whoever doesn’t receive you or hear your words, as
you go out of that house or that city,

586
00:45:18,494 --> 00:45:20,194
shake the dust off your feet.

587
00:45:21,014 --> 00:45:27,004
Most certainly I tell you, it will be
more tolerable for the land of Sodom and Gomorrah

588
00:45:27,044 --> 00:45:29,864
in the day of judgement than for that
city.

589
00:45:30,584 --> 00:45:34,064
“Behold, I send you out as sheep amongst
wolves.

590
00:45:34,704 --> 00:45:38,844
Therefore be wise as serpents and harmless
as doves.

591
00:45:39,604 --> 00:45:45,284
But beware of men, for they will deliver
you up to councils, and in their synagogues

592
00:45:45,324 --> 00:45:46,484
they will scourge you.

593
00:45:46,924 --> 00:45:52,984
Yes, and you will be brought before governors
and kings for my sake, for a testimony

594
00:45:53,024 --> 00:45:54,604
to them and to the nations.

595
00:45:55,684 --> 00:46:01,624
But when they deliver you up, don’t be anxious
how or what you will say, for it will

596
00:46:01,664 --> 00:46:04,204
be given you in that hour what you will
say.

597
00:46:04,724 --> 00:46:10,024
For it is not you who speak, but the
Spirit of your Father who speaks in you.

598
00:46:10,418 --> 00:46:14,759
“Brother will deliver up brother to death,
and the father his child.

599
00:46:15,759 --> 00:46:20,538
Children will rise up against parents and
cause them to be put to death.

600
00:46:21,518 --> 00:46:28,018
You will be hated by all men for my name’s
sake, but he who endures to the end will be

601
00:46:28,058 --> 00:46:28,958
saved.

602
00:46:28,998 --> 00:46:35,199
But when they persecute you in this city,
flee into the next, for most certainly I tell

603
00:46:35,239 --> 00:46:40,598
you, you will not have gone through the cities
of Israel until the Son of Man has come.

604
00:46:41,938 --> 00:46:46,379
“A disciple is not above his teacher, nor
a servant above his lord.

605
00:46:47,158 --> 00:46:52,138
It is enough for the disciple that he be
like his teacher, and the servant like his lord.

606
00:46:53,118 --> 00:46:58,739
If they have called the master of the
house Beelzebul, how much more those of his household!

607
00:46:59,638 --> 00:47:04,819
Therefore don’t be afraid of them, for there
is nothing covered that will not be revealed,

608
00:47:05,379 --> 00:47:07,558
or hidden that will not be known.

609
00:47:08,779 --> 00:47:14,659
What I tell you in the darkness, speak in
the light; and what you hear whispered in the

610
00:47:14,699 --> 00:47:17,158
ear, proclaim on the housetops.

611
00:47:17,739 --> 00:47:22,618
Don’t be afraid of those who kill the
body, but are not able to kill the soul.

612
00:47:23,779 --> 00:47:29,078
Rather, fear him who is able to destroy
both soul and body in Gehenna.

613
00:47:29,859 --> 00:47:33,058
“Aren’t two sparrows sold for an assarion
coin?

614
00:47:33,918 --> 00:47:37,558
Not one of them falls to the ground apart
from your Father’s will.

615
00:47:38,118 --> 00:47:40,658
But the very hairs of your head are all
numbered.

616
00:47:41,839 --> 00:47:43,219
Therefore don’t be afraid.

617
00:47:44,219 --> 00:47:46,739
You are of more value than many sparrows.

618
00:47:47,319 --> 00:47:53,799
Everyone therefore who confesses me before men,
I will also confess him before my Father

619
00:47:53,839 --> 00:47:54,998
who is in heaven.

620
00:47:55,658 --> 00:48:02,219
But whoever denies me before men, I will also
deny him before my Father who is in heaven.

621
00:48:03,458 --> 00:48:06,399
“Don’t think that I came to send peace on
the earth.

622
00:48:07,199 --> 00:48:09,918
I didn’t come to send peace, but a sword.

623
00:48:10,538 --> 00:48:16,219
For I came to set a man at odds
against his father, and a daughter against her mother,

624
00:48:16,638 --> 00:48:20,179
and a daughter-in-law against her
mother-in-law.

625
00:48:20,219 --> 00:48:23,558
A man’s foes will be those of his own
household.

626
00:48:24,518 --> 00:48:31,038
He who loves father or mother more than me
is not worthy of me; and he who loves son

627
00:48:31,078 --> 00:48:34,239
or daughter more than me isn’t worthy of
me.

628
00:48:34,565 --> 00:48:39,505
He who doesn’t take his cross and follow
after me isn’t worthy of me.

629
00:48:40,385 --> 00:48:46,965
He who seeks his life will lose it; and he
who loses his life for my sake will find it.

630
00:48:48,145 --> 00:48:54,385
“He who receives you receives me, and he
who receives me receives him who sent me.

631
00:48:54,865 --> 00:48:59,705
He who receives a prophet in the name of a
prophet will receive a prophet’s reward.

632
00:49:00,525 --> 00:49:06,245
He who receives a righteous man in the
name of a righteous man will receive a righteous

633
00:49:06,285 --> 00:49:07,225
man’s reward.

634
00:49:07,845 --> 00:49:14,045
Whoever gives one of these little ones just a
cup of cold water to drink in the name

635
00:49:14,085 --> 00:49:20,605
of a disciple, most certainly I tell you,
he will in no way lose his reward.”

636
00:49:21,785 --> 00:49:24,085
Matthew, chapter eleven.

637
00:49:24,125 --> 00:49:29,605
When Jesus had finished directing his twelve
disciples, he departed from there to teach

638
00:49:29,645 --> 00:49:31,025
and preach in their cities.

639
00:49:32,125 --> 00:49:37,765
Now when John heard in the prison the works
of Christ, he sent two of his disciples and

640
00:49:37,805 --> 00:49:42,525
said to him, “Are you he who comes, or
should we look for another?”

641
00:49:43,285 --> 00:49:49,805
Jesus answered them, “Go and tell John the
things which you hear and see: the blind receive

642
00:49:49,845 --> 00:49:56,345
their sight, the lame walk, the lepers are
cleansed, the deaf hear, the dead

643
00:49:56,385 --> 00:49:59,965
are raised up, and the poor have good news
preached to them.

644
00:50:00,745 --> 00:50:04,345
Blessed is he who finds no occasion for
stumbling in me.”

645
00:50:04,905 --> 00:50:11,565
As these went their way, Jesus began
to say to the multitudes concerning John, “What

646
00:50:11,605 --> 00:50:13,965
did you go out into the wilderness to see?

647
00:50:14,845 --> 00:50:16,385
A reed shaken by the wind?

648
00:50:17,205 --> 00:50:19,025
But what did you go out to see?

649
00:50:19,885 --> 00:50:21,225
A man in soft clothing?

650
00:50:21,825 --> 00:50:26,005
Behold, those who wear soft clothing are
in kings’ houses.

651
00:50:26,725 --> 00:50:28,065
But why did you go out?

652
00:50:28,105 --> 00:50:29,585
To see a prophet?

653
00:50:30,225 --> 00:50:33,605
Yes, I tell you, and much more than a
prophet.

654
00:50:34,345 --> 00:50:40,605
For this is he, of whom it is
written, ‘Behold, I send my messenger before your face,

655
00:50:41,205 --> 00:50:43,425
who will prepare your way before you.’

656
00:50:44,025 --> 00:50:50,225
Most certainly I tell you, amongst those who
are born of women there has not arisen anyone

657
00:50:50,265 --> 00:50:56,665
greater than John the Baptiser; yet he who
is least in the Kingdom of Heaven is greater

658
00:50:56,705 --> 00:50:57,579
than he.

659
00:50:57,619 --> 00:51:03,879
From the days of John the Baptiser
until now, the Kingdom of Heaven suffers violence,

660
00:51:04,519 --> 00:51:06,739
and the violent take it by force.

661
00:51:07,899 --> 00:51:11,639
For all the prophets and the law
prophesied until John.

662
00:51:12,139 --> 00:51:16,639
If you are willing to receive it, this is
Elijah, who is to come.

663
00:51:17,739 --> 00:51:20,719
He who has ears to hear, let him hear.

664
00:51:21,359 --> 00:51:23,439
“But to what shall I compare this
generation?

665
00:51:24,679 --> 00:51:30,459
It is like children sitting in the
marketplaces, who call to their companions and say,

666
00:51:31,559 --> 00:51:34,319
‘We played the flute for you, and you
didn’t dance.

667
00:51:35,199 --> 00:51:37,499
We mourned for you, and you didn’t
lament.’

668
00:51:38,259 --> 00:51:43,479
For John came neither eating nor drinking,
and they say, ‘He has a demon.’

669
00:51:44,699 --> 00:51:51,619
The Son of Man came eating and drinking,
and they say, ‘Behold, a gluttonous man and

670
00:51:51,659 --> 00:51:54,959
a drunkard, a friend of tax collectors and
sinners!’

671
00:51:56,279 --> 00:51:58,659
But wisdom is justified by her children.”

672
00:51:59,259 --> 00:52:04,539
Then he began to denounce the cities in
which most of his mighty works had been done,

673
00:52:05,059 --> 00:52:06,559
because they didn’t repent.

674
00:52:07,719 --> 00:52:10,359
“Woe to you, Chorazin!

675
00:52:10,399 --> 00:52:12,059
Woe to you, Bethsaida!

676
00:52:12,759 --> 00:52:17,999
For if the mighty works had been done in
Tyre and Sidon which were done in you, they

677
00:52:18,039 --> 00:52:21,239
would have repented long ago in sackcloth
and ashes.

678
00:52:22,219 --> 00:52:27,839
But I tell you, it will be more tolerable
for Tyre and Sidon on the day of judgement

679
00:52:27,879 --> 00:52:28,979
than for you.

680
00:52:29,459 --> 00:52:34,979
You, Capernaum, who are exalted to heaven,
you will go down to Hades.

681
00:52:35,699 --> 00:52:41,459
For if the mighty works had been done in
Sodom which were done in you, it would have

682
00:52:41,499 --> 00:52:42,899
remained until today.

683
00:52:43,239 --> 00:52:48,819
But I tell you that it will be more tolerable
for the land of Sodom on the day of judgement,

684
00:52:48,859 --> 00:52:50,119
than for you.”

685
00:52:50,759 --> 00:52:57,339
At that time, Jesus answered, “I thank
you, Father, Lord of heaven and earth, that

686
00:52:57,379 --> 00:53:02,459
you hid these things from the wise
and understanding, and revealed them to infants.

687
00:53:03,599 --> 00:53:07,499
Yes, Father, for so it was well-pleasing
in your sight.

688
00:53:08,259 --> 00:53:11,299
All things have been delivered to me by my
Father.

689
00:53:11,739 --> 00:53:18,239
No one knows the Son, except the
Father; neither does anyone know the Father, except

690
00:53:18,279 --> 00:53:22,359
the Son and he to whom the Son desires to
reveal him.

691
00:53:22,671 --> 00:53:28,451
“Come to me, all you who labour and
are heavily burdened, and I will give you rest.

692
00:53:29,451 --> 00:53:36,311
Take my yoke upon you and learn from me,
for I am gentle and humble in heart; and

693
00:53:36,351 --> 00:53:38,271
you will find rest for your souls.

694
00:53:38,811 --> 00:53:41,891
For my yoke is easy, and my burden is
light.”

695
00:53:42,991 --> 00:53:45,671
Matthew, chapter twelve.

696
00:53:45,711 --> 00:53:50,611
At that time, Jesus went on the Sabbath
day through the grain fields.

697
00:53:51,271 --> 00:53:56,331
His disciples were hungry and began to
pluck heads of grain and to eat.

698
00:53:57,331 --> 00:54:03,871
But the Pharisees, when they saw it, said
to him, “Behold, your disciples do what is

699
00:54:03,911 --> 00:54:05,811
not lawful to do on the Sabbath.”

700
00:54:06,351 --> 00:54:12,211
But he said to them, “Haven’t you read what
David did when he was hungry, and those who

701
00:54:12,251 --> 00:54:18,131
were with him: how he entered into God’s
house and ate the show bread, which was not

702
00:54:18,171 --> 00:54:23,691
lawful for him to eat, nor for those who
were with him, but only for the priests?

703
00:54:24,311 --> 00:54:29,611
Or have you not read in the law that
on the Sabbath day the priests in the temple profane

704
00:54:29,651 --> 00:54:31,451
the Sabbath and are guiltless?

705
00:54:32,151 --> 00:54:35,511
But I tell you that one greater than the
temple is here.

706
00:54:36,051 --> 00:54:42,391
But if you had known what this means,
‘I desire mercy, and not sacrifice,’ you wouldn’t

707
00:54:42,431 --> 00:54:43,991
have condemned the guiltless.

708
00:54:44,291 --> 00:54:47,111
For the Son of Man is Lord of the
Sabbath.”

709
00:54:48,131 --> 00:54:51,251
He departed from there and went into their
synagogue.

710
00:54:51,911 --> 00:54:55,291
And behold, there was a man with a
withered hand.

711
00:54:55,971 --> 00:54:59,991
They asked him, “Is it lawful to heal on
the Sabbath day?”

712
00:55:00,031 --> 00:55:02,131
so that they might accuse him.

713
00:55:03,131 --> 00:55:09,651
He said to them, “What man is there amongst
you who has one sheep, and if this one

714
00:55:09,691 --> 00:55:15,131
falls into a pit on the Sabbath day, won’t
he grab on to it and lift it out?

715
00:55:15,171 --> 00:55:18,891
Of how much more value then is a man than
a sheep!

716
00:55:19,891 --> 00:55:23,231
Therefore it is lawful to do good on the
Sabbath day.”

717
00:55:24,171 --> 00:55:27,171
Then he told the man, “Stretch out your
hand.”

718
00:55:28,071 --> 00:55:32,591
He stretched it out; and it was restored
whole, just like the other.

719
00:55:33,131 --> 00:55:38,451
But the Pharisees went out and conspired
against him, how they might destroy him.

720
00:55:39,471 --> 00:55:42,851
Jesus, perceiving that, withdrew from
there.

721
00:55:43,121 --> 00:55:49,121
Great multitudes followed him; and he healed
them all, and commanded them that they should

722
00:55:49,161 --> 00:55:55,081
not make him known, that it might be
fulfilled which was spoken through Isaiah the prophet,

723
00:55:55,521 --> 00:56:02,161
saying, “Behold, my servant whom I have
chosen, my beloved in whom my soul is well

724
00:56:02,201 --> 00:56:03,101
pleased.

725
00:56:03,261 --> 00:56:05,041
I will put my Spirit on him.

726
00:56:05,601 --> 00:56:07,941
He will proclaim justice to the nations.

727
00:56:08,681 --> 00:56:14,281
He will not strive, nor shout, neither
will anyone hear his voice in the streets.

728
00:56:15,181 --> 00:56:17,061
He won’t break a bruised reed.

729
00:56:17,521 --> 00:56:21,941
He won’t quench a smoking flax, until he
leads justice to victory.

730
00:56:22,901 --> 00:56:25,121
In his name, the nations will hope.”

731
00:56:25,801 --> 00:56:32,141
Then one possessed by a demon, blind and
mute, was brought to him; and he healed him,

732
00:56:32,181 --> 00:56:39,881
so that

733
00:56:39,921 --> 00:56:40,221
the blind and mute man both spoke and saw.

734
00:56:40,261 --> 00:56:41,821
All the multitudes were amazed, and said,
“Can this be the son of David?”

735
00:56:42,481 --> 00:56:48,381
But when the Pharisees heard it, they said,
“This man does not cast out demons except

736
00:56:48,421 --> 00:56:51,021
by Beelzebul, the prince of the demons.”

737
00:56:51,641 --> 00:56:57,661
Knowing their thoughts, Jesus said to
them, “Every kingdom divided against itself is

738
00:56:57,701 --> 00:57:03,861
brought to desolation, and every city or
house divided against itself will not stand.

739
00:57:04,821 --> 00:57:08,681
If Satan casts out Satan, he is divided
against himself.

740
00:57:09,321 --> 00:57:11,501
How then will his kingdom stand?

741
00:57:12,201 --> 00:57:17,941
If I by Beelzebul cast out demons, by whom
do your children cast them out?

742
00:57:18,701 --> 00:57:20,441
Therefore they will be your judges.

743
00:57:21,381 --> 00:57:27,301
But if I by the Spirit of God cast
out demons, then God’s Kingdom has come upon you.

744
00:57:27,741 --> 00:57:33,441
Or how can one enter into the house of
the strong man and plunder his goods, unless he

745
00:57:33,481 --> 00:57:35,161
first bind the strong man?

746
00:57:35,861 --> 00:57:37,501
Then he will plunder his house.

747
00:57:38,681 --> 00:57:44,041
“He who is not with me is against me, and
he who doesn’t gather with me, scatters.

748
00:57:44,941 --> 00:57:50,821
Therefore I tell you, every sin and
blasphemy will be forgiven men, but the blasphemy

749
00:57:50,861 --> 00:57:53,741
against the Spirit will not be forgiven
men.

750
00:57:54,098 --> 00:58:00,878
Whoever speaks a word against the Son of
Man, it will be forgiven him; but whoever speaks

751
00:58:00,918 --> 00:58:07,618
against the Holy Spirit, it will not be
forgiven him, either in this age, or in that

752
00:58:07,658 --> 00:58:08,558
which is to come.

753
00:58:08,898 --> 00:58:15,018
“Either make the tree good and its fruit
good, or make the tree corrupt and its fruit

754
00:58:15,058 --> 00:58:18,138
corrupt; for the tree is known by its
fruit.

755
00:58:18,918 --> 00:58:25,178
You offspring of vipers, how can you,
being evil, speak good things?

756
00:58:26,298 --> 00:58:29,598
For out of the abundance of the heart, the
mouth speaks.

757
00:58:30,258 --> 00:58:36,138
The good man out of his good treasure brings
out good things, and the evil man out of

758
00:58:36,178 --> 00:58:38,838
his evil treasure brings out evil things.

759
00:58:39,638 --> 00:58:45,218
I tell you that every idle word that men
speak, they will give account of it in the day

760
00:58:45,258 --> 00:58:46,458
of judgement.

761
00:58:46,498 --> 00:58:51,718
For by your words you will be justified,
and by your words you will be condemned.”

762
00:58:53,138 --> 00:58:59,558
Then certain of the scribes and Pharisees answered,
“Teacher, we want to see a sign from

763
00:58:59,598 --> 00:59:00,278
you.”

764
00:59:00,318 --> 00:59:07,038
But he answered them, “An evil and
adulterous generation seeks after a sign, but

765
00:59:07,078 --> 00:59:11,218
no sign will be given to it but the sign
of Jonah the prophet.

766
00:59:11,258 --> 00:59:17,838
For as Jonah was three days and three nights
in the belly of the huge fish, so will the

767
00:59:17,878 --> 00:59:21,518
Son of Man be three days and three nights
in the heart of the earth.

768
00:59:22,578 --> 00:59:27,818
The men of Nineveh will stand up in
the judgement with this generation and will condemn

769
00:59:27,858 --> 00:59:34,218
it, for they repented at the preaching
of Jonah; and behold, someone greater than Jonah

770
00:59:34,258 --> 00:59:35,158
is here.

771
00:59:35,758 --> 00:59:41,678
The Queen of the South will rise up
in the judgement with this generation and will condemn

772
00:59:41,718 --> 00:59:48,398
it, for she came from the ends of the
earth to hear the wisdom of Solomon; and behold,

773
00:59:49,178 --> 00:59:51,198
someone greater than Solomon is here.

774
00:59:51,878 --> 00:59:57,938
“When an unclean spirit has gone out of
a man, he passes through waterless places seeking

775
00:59:57,978 --> 01:00:00,058
rest, and doesn’t find it.

776
01:00:01,058 --> 01:00:07,858
Then he says, ‘I will return into my house
from which I came;’ and when he has come back,

777
01:00:08,238 --> 01:00:11,598
he finds it empty, swept, and put in
order.

778
01:00:11,935 --> 01:00:18,075
Then he goes and takes with himself seven
other spirits more evil than he is, and they

779
01:00:18,115 --> 01:00:19,975
enter in and dwell there.

780
01:00:21,095 --> 01:00:24,395
The last state of that man becomes worse
than the first.

781
01:00:25,115 --> 01:00:28,535
Even so will it be also to this evil
generation.”

782
01:00:29,475 --> 01:00:41,215
While he was yet speaking to the
multitudes, behold, his mother and

783
01:00:41,255 --> 01:00:41,555
his brothers stood outside, seeking to
speak to him.

784
01:00:41,595 --> 01:00:45,075
One said to him, “Behold, your mother
and your brothers stand outside, seeking to speak

785
01:00:45,115 --> 01:00:45,975
to you.”

786
01:00:46,015 --> 01:00:49,555
But he answered him who spoke to him, “Who
is my mother?

787
01:00:50,155 --> 01:00:51,055
Who are my brothers?”

788
01:00:51,895 --> 01:00:58,235
He stretched out his hand towards his
disciples, and said, “Behold, my mother and my

789
01:00:58,275 --> 01:00:59,175
brothers!

790
01:00:59,355 --> 01:01:04,995
For whoever does the will of my Father who
is in heaven, he is my brother, and sister,

791
01:01:05,035 --> 01:01:05,935
and mother.”

792
01:01:06,755 --> 01:01:08,855
Matthew, chapter thirteen.

793
01:01:08,895 --> 01:01:13,595
On that day Jesus went out of the house
and sat by the seaside.

794
01:01:14,415 --> 01:01:20,975
Great multitudes gathered to him, so that
he entered into a boat and sat; and all

795
01:01:21,015 --> 01:01:22,815
the multitude stood on the beach.

796
01:01:23,315 --> 01:01:29,695
He spoke to them many things in parables,
saying, “Behold, a farmer went out to sow.

797
01:01:30,335 --> 01:01:41,135
As he sowed, some seeds fell by the
roadside, and the

798
01:01:41,175 --> 01:01:41,475
birds came and devoured them.

799
01:01:41,515 --> 01:01:42,915
Others fell on rocky ground, where they
didn’t have much soil, and immediately they sprang

800
01:01:42,955 --> 01:01:45,655
up, because they had no depth of earth.

801
01:01:46,615 --> 01:01:49,135
When the sun had risen, they were
scorched.

802
01:01:49,495 --> 01:01:52,515
Because they had no root, they withered
away.

803
01:01:53,375 --> 01:01:55,115
Others fell amongst thorns.

804
01:01:55,995 --> 01:01:57,935
The thorns grew up and choked them.

805
01:01:58,715 --> 01:02:05,335
Others fell on good soil and yielded fruit:
some one hundred times as much, some sixty,

806
01:02:05,995 --> 01:02:06,895
and some thirty.

807
01:02:07,115 --> 01:02:09,975
He who has ears to hear, let him hear.”

808
01:02:10,615 --> 01:02:15,775
The disciples came, and said to him, “Why
do you speak to them in parables?”

809
01:02:16,695 --> 01:02:21,815
He answered them, “To you it is given
to know the mysteries of the Kingdom of Heaven,

810
01:02:22,755 --> 01:02:24,275
but it is not given to them.

811
01:02:25,115 --> 01:02:31,215
For whoever has, to him will be given,
and he will have abundance; but whoever doesn’t

812
01:02:31,255 --> 01:02:36,175
have, from him will be taken away even
that which he has.

813
01:02:36,494 --> 01:02:43,054
Therefore I speak to them in parables,
because seeing they don’t see, and hearing, they

814
01:02:43,094 --> 01:02:45,674
don’t hear, neither do they understand.

815
01:02:47,034 --> 01:02:54,114
In them the prophecy of Isaiah is fulfilled,
which says, ‘By hearing you will hear, and

816
01:02:54,154 --> 01:03:01,394
will in no way understand; Seeing you will
see, and will in no way perceive; for

817
01:03:01,434 --> 01:03:06,894
this people’s heart has grown callous, their
ears are dull of hearing, and they have

818
01:03:06,934 --> 01:03:12,734
closed their eyes; or else perhaps they
might perceive with their eyes, hear with their

819
01:03:12,774 --> 01:03:18,154
ears, understand with their heart, and
would turn again, and I would heal them.’

820
01:03:18,834 --> 01:03:23,534
“But blessed are your eyes, for they see;
and your ears, for they hear.

821
01:03:24,354 --> 01:03:29,874
For most certainly I tell you that many
prophets and righteous men desired to see the

822
01:03:29,914 --> 01:03:35,354
things which you see, and didn’t see them;
and to hear the things which you hear, and

823
01:03:35,394 --> 01:03:36,294
didn’t hear them.

824
01:03:36,714 --> 01:03:38,794
“Hear, then, the parable of the farmer.

825
01:03:39,774 --> 01:03:45,454
When anyone hears the word of the Kingdom
and doesn’t understand it, the evil one comes

826
01:03:45,494 --> 01:03:49,174
and snatches away that which has been sown
in his heart.

827
01:03:50,014 --> 01:03:52,174
This is what was sown by the roadside.

828
01:03:52,834 --> 01:03:59,434
What was sown on the rocky places, this is
he who hears the word and immediately with

829
01:03:59,474 --> 01:04:05,474
joy receives it; yet he has no root in
himself, but endures for a while.

830
01:04:06,374 --> 01:04:12,094
When oppression or persecution arises because
of the word, immediately he stumbles.

831
01:04:12,854 --> 01:04:19,434
What was sown amongst the thorns, this is he
who hears the word, but the cares of this

832
01:04:19,474 --> 01:04:25,394
age and the deceitfulness of riches choke
the word, and he becomes unfruitful.

833
01:04:25,834 --> 01:04:32,234
What was sown on the good ground, this is
he who hears the word and understands it, who

834
01:04:32,274 --> 01:04:38,614
most certainly bears fruit and produces, some
one hundred times as much, some sixty,

835
01:04:38,654 --> 01:04:40,694
and some thirty.”

836
01:04:40,734 --> 01:04:46,234
He set another parable before them, saying, “The
Kingdom of Heaven is like a man who

837
01:04:46,274 --> 01:04:52,694
sowed good seed in his field, but while
people slept, his enemy came and sowed darnel

838
01:04:52,734 --> 01:04:55,694
weeds also amongst the wheat, and went
away.

839
01:04:56,053 --> 01:05:02,073
But when the blade sprang up and
produced grain, then the darnel weeds appeared also.

840
01:05:03,333 --> 01:05:09,853
The servants of the householder came and said
to him, ‘Sir, didn’t you sow good seed

841
01:05:09,893 --> 01:05:10,793
in your field?

842
01:05:11,593 --> 01:05:13,773
Where did these darnel weeds come from?’

843
01:05:14,173 --> 01:05:17,153
“He said to them, ‘An enemy has done
this.’

844
01:05:17,753 --> 01:05:21,853
“The servants asked him, ‘Do you want us
to go and gather them up?’

845
01:05:22,433 --> 01:05:29,033
“But he said, ‘No, lest perhaps while you
gather up the darnel weeds, you root

846
01:05:29,073 --> 01:05:30,333
up the wheat with them.

847
01:05:30,793 --> 01:05:36,433
Let both grow together until the harvest, and
in the harvest time I will tell the reapers,

848
01:05:37,833 --> 01:05:43,393
“First, gather up the darnel weeds, and bind
them in bundles to burn them; but gather

849
01:05:43,433 --> 01:05:49,693
the wheat into my barn.”’” He set
another parable before them, saying, “The Kingdom of

850
01:05:49,733 --> 01:05:55,833
Heaven is like a grain of mustard seed which
a man took, and sowed in his field, which

851
01:05:55,873 --> 01:05:57,773
indeed is smaller than all seeds.

852
01:05:58,633 --> 01:06:04,613
But when it is grown, it is greater than
the herbs and becomes a tree, so that the birds

853
01:06:04,653 --> 01:06:07,053
of the air come and lodge in its
branches.”

854
01:06:08,373 --> 01:06:10,313
He spoke another parable to them.

855
01:06:10,753 --> 01:06:16,453
