03:01:26,977 --> 03:01:33,097
The former insincerely preach Christ from
selfish ambition, thinking that they add affliction

2304
03:01:33,137 --> 03:01:39,277
to my chains; but the latter out of
love, knowing that I am appointed for the defence

2305
03:01:39,317 --> 03:01:40,297
of the Good News.

2306
03:01:41,137 --> 03:01:42,257
What does it matter?

2307
03:01:42,690 --> 03:01:48,750
Only that in every way, whether in
pretence or in truth, Christ is proclaimed.

2308
03:01:50,370 --> 03:01:53,930
I rejoice in this, yes, and will rejoice.

2309
03:01:54,590 --> 03:02:00,190
For I know that this will turn out
to my salvation through your prayers and the supply

2310
03:02:00,231 --> 03:02:06,670
of the Spirit of Jesus Christ, according to
my earnest expectation and hope, that I will

2311
03:02:06,711 --> 03:02:13,390
in no way be disappointed, but with all
boldness, as always, now also Christ

2312
03:02:13,430 --> 03:02:18,211
will be magnified in my body, whether by
life or by death.

2313
03:02:18,570 --> 03:02:22,090
For to me to live is Christ, and to die is
gain.

2314
03:02:23,131 --> 03:02:29,190
But if I live on in the flesh, this will
bring fruit from my work; yet I don’t know what

2315
03:02:29,231 --> 03:02:30,131
I will choose.

2316
03:02:30,610 --> 03:02:37,510
But I

2317
03:02:37,551 --> 03:02:38,737
am hard pressed between the two, having the
desire to depart and be with Christ, which

2318
03:02:38,777 --> 03:02:39,077
is far better.

2319
03:02:39,117 --> 03:02:42,631
Yet to remain in the flesh is more needful
for your sake.

2320
03:02:43,291 --> 03:02:49,890
Having this confidence, I know that I will
remain, yes, and remain with you all

2321
03:02:49,930 --> 03:02:55,890
for your progress and joy in the faith,
that your boasting may abound in Christ Jesus

2322
03:02:55,930 --> 03:02:58,750
in me through my presence with you again.

2323
03:02:59,330 --> 03:03:05,330
Only let your way of life be worthy of
the Good News of Christ, that whether I come and

2324
03:03:05,370 --> 03:03:11,950
see you or am absent, I may hear of your
state, that you stand firm in one spirit,

2325
03:03:11,990 --> 03:03:18,110
with one soul striving for the faith of
the Good News; and in nothing frightened by the

2326
03:03:18,150 --> 03:03:25,010
adversaries, which is for them a proof of
destruction, but to you of salvation, and

2327
03:03:25,051 --> 03:03:25,950
that from God.

2328
03:03:26,391 --> 03:03:32,570
Because it has been granted to you on behalf
of Christ, not only to believe in him, but

2329
03:03:32,610 --> 03:03:39,070
also to suffer on his behalf, having the
same conflict which you saw in me and now

2330
03:03:39,110 --> 03:03:40,190
hear is in me.

2331
03:03:41,430 --> 03:03:42,490
Philippians, chapter two.

2332
03:03:43,351 --> 03:03:50,131
If therefore there is any exhortation in
Christ, if any consolation of love, if

2333
03:03:50,171 --> 03:03:56,851
any fellowship of the Spirit, if any
tender mercies and compassion, make my joy

2334
03:03:56,891 --> 03:04:03,471
full by being like-minded, having the same
love, being of one accord, of

2335
03:04:03,511 --> 03:04:10,391
one mind; doing nothing through rivalry or
through conceit, but in humility, each

2336
03:04:10,431 --> 03:04:16,131
counting others better than himself; each
of you not just looking to his own things,

2337
03:04:16,891 --> 03:04:19,391
but each of you also to the things of
others.

2338
03:04:20,031 --> 03:04:26,571
Have this in your mind, which was also in
Christ Jesus, who, existing in the form of

2339
03:04:26,611 --> 03:04:33,451
God, didn’t consider equality with God a
thing to be grasped, but emptied himself, taking

2340
03:04:33,491 --> 03:04:37,181
the form of a servant, being made in the
likeness of men.

2341
03:04:37,801 --> 03:04:44,041
And being found in human form, he humbled
himself, becoming obedient to the point of

2342
03:04:44,081 --> 03:04:47,141
death, yes, the death of the cross.

2343
03:04:47,821 --> 03:04:53,781
Therefore God also highly exalted him, and
gave to him the name which is above every

2344
03:04:53,821 --> 03:05:00,401
name, that at the name of Jesus every knee
should bow, of those in heaven, those on

2345
03:05:00,441 --> 03:05:06,201
earth, and those under the earth, and
that every tongue should confess that Jesus Christ

2346
03:05:06,241 --> 03:05:09,241
is Lord, to the glory of God the Father.

2347
03:05:09,721 --> 03:05:16,561
So then, my beloved, even as you have
always obeyed, not only in my presence, but

2348
03:05:16,601 --> 03:05:22,661
now much more in my absence, work out your
own salvation with fear and trembling.

2349
03:05:23,421 --> 03:05:29,121
For it is God who works in you both to
will and to work for his good pleasure.

2350
03:05:30,101 --> 03:05:35,301
Do all things without complaining and arguing,
that you may become blameless and harmless,

2351
03:05:36,001 --> 03:05:42,061
children of God without defect in the
middle of a crooked and perverse generation, amongst

2352
03:05:42,101 --> 03:05:47,941
whom you are seen as lights in the world,
holding up the word of life, that I may have

2353
03:05:47,981 --> 03:05:53,921
something to boast in the day of Christ that
I didn’t run in vain nor labour in vain.

2354
03:05:54,701 --> 03:06:01,241
Yes, and if I am poured out on the
sacrifice and service of your faith, I am glad and

2355
03:06:01,281 --> 03:06:02,561
rejoice with you all.

2356
03:06:03,281 --> 03:06:07,361
In the same way, you also should be glad
and rejoice with me.

2357
03:06:07,710 --> 03:06:14,030
But I hope in the Lord Jesus to send
Timothy to you soon, that I also may be cheered

2358
03:06:14,070 --> 03:06:16,330
up when I know how you are doing.

2359
03:06:17,190 --> 03:06:21,850
For I have no one else like-minded, who
will truly care about you.

2360
03:06:22,250 --> 03:06:26,170
For they all seek their own, not the
things of Jesus Christ.

2361
03:06:26,910 --> 03:06:29,910
But you know that he has proved himself.

2362
03:06:29,950 --> 03:06:36,410
As a child serves a father, so he served
with me in furtherance of the Good News.

2363
03:06:37,410 --> 03:06:42,730
Therefore I hope to send him at once, as
soon as I see how it will go with me.

2364
03:06:43,650 --> 03:06:48,010
But I trust in the Lord that I myself also
will come shortly.

2365
03:06:48,590 --> 03:06:55,570
But I thought it necessary to send
to you Epaphroditus, my brother, fellow worker, fellow

2366
03:06:55,610 --> 03:07:02,090
soldier, and your apostle and servant of my
need, since he longed for you all, and was

2367
03:07:02,130 --> 03:07:05,230
very troubled because you had heard that
he was sick.

2368
03:07:05,270 --> 03:07:11,730
For indeed he was sick nearly to death,
but God had mercy on him, and not

2369
03:07:11,770 --> 03:07:17,770
on him only, but on me also, that I might
not have sorrow on sorrow.

2370
03:07:18,230 --> 03:07:24,010
I have sent him therefore the more diligently,
that when you see him again, you may rejoice,

2371
03:07:24,750 --> 03:07:27,070
and that I may be the less sorrowful.

2372
03:07:27,610 --> 03:07:34,210
Receive him therefore in the Lord with all
joy, and hold such people in honour, because

2373
03:07:34,250 --> 03:07:40,470
for the work of Christ he came near to
death, risking his life to supply that which was

2374
03:07:40,510 --> 03:07:42,570
lacking in your service towards me.

2375
03:07:43,990 --> 03:07:46,550
Philippians, chapter three.

2376
03:07:46,590 --> 03:07:49,950
Finally, my brothers, rejoice in the Lord!

2377
03:07:50,610 --> 03:07:57,270
To write the same things to you, to me
indeed is not tiresome, but for you it

2378
03:07:57,310 --> 03:07:58,210
is safe.

2379
03:07:58,290 --> 03:08:04,230
Beware of the dogs; beware of the evil
workers; beware of the false circumcision.

2380
03:08:05,490 --> 03:08:11,710
For we are the circumcision, who worship God
in the Spirit, and rejoice in Christ Jesus,

2381
03:08:12,410 --> 03:08:18,230
and have no confidence in the flesh; though
I myself might have confidence even in the

2382
03:08:18,270 --> 03:08:18,887
flesh.

2383
03:08:18,927 --> 03:08:25,767
If any other man thinks that he has
confidence in the flesh, I yet more: circumcised

2384
03:08:25,807 --> 03:08:32,587
the eighth day, of the stock of Israel,
of the tribe of Benjamin, a Hebrew of Hebrews;

2385
03:08:33,407 --> 03:08:40,527
concerning the law, a Pharisee; concerning
zeal, persecuting the assembly; concerning

2386
03:08:40,567 --> 03:08:44,267
the righteousness which is in the law,
found blameless.

2387
03:08:45,187 --> 03:08:50,747
However, I consider those things that were
gain to me as a loss for Christ.

2388
03:08:51,787 --> 03:08:57,747
Yes most certainly, and I count all things to
be a loss for the excellency of the knowledge

2389
03:08:57,787 --> 03:09:03,827
of Christ Jesus, my Lord, for whom I
suffered the loss of all things, and count them

2390
03:09:03,867 --> 03:09:10,567
nothing but refuse, that I may gain Christ
and be found in him, not having a righteousness

2391
03:09:10,607 --> 03:09:17,487
of my own, that which is of the law,
but that which is through faith in Christ, the righteousness

2392
03:09:17,527 --> 03:09:24,147
which is from God by faith, that I may
know him and the power of his resurrection, and

2393
03:09:24,187 --> 03:09:30,647
the fellowship of his sufferings, becoming
conformed to his death, if by any means

2394
03:09:30,687 --> 03:09:33,567
I may attain to the resurrection from the
dead.

2395
03:09:34,367 --> 03:09:40,847
Not that I have already obtained, or am
already made perfect; but I press on, that

2396
03:09:40,887 --> 03:09:45,707
I may take hold of that for which also I
was taken hold of by Christ Jesus.

2397
03:09:46,347 --> 03:09:53,447
Brothers, I don’t regard myself as yet having
taken hold, but one thing I do: forgetting

2398
03:09:53,487 --> 03:09:59,287
the things which are behind and stretching
forward to the things which are before, I

2399
03:09:59,327 --> 03:10:04,647
press on towards the goal for the prize of
the high calling of God in Christ Jesus.

2400
03:10:05,327 --> 03:10:09,147
Let us therefore, as many as are perfect,
think this way.

2401
03:10:09,887 --> 03:10:14,767
If in anything you think otherwise, God
will also reveal that to you.

2402
03:10:15,707 --> 03:10:21,687
Nevertheless, to the extent that we have
already attained, let’s walk by the same rule.

2403
03:10:22,607 --> 03:10:23,987
Let’s be of the same mind.

2404
03:10:24,927 --> 03:10:31,427
Brothers, be imitators together of me, and
note those who walk this way, even as you

2405
03:10:31,467 --> 03:10:32,867
have us for an example.

2406
03:10:33,276 --> 03:10:39,736
For many walk, of whom I told you often,
and now tell you even weeping, as

2407
03:10:39,776 --> 03:10:46,116
the enemies of the cross of Christ, whose
end is destruction, whose god is the belly,

2408
03:10:46,636 --> 03:10:51,136
and whose glory is in their shame, who
think about earthly things.

2409
03:10:51,896 --> 03:10:58,036
For our citizenship is in heaven, from where
we also wait for a Saviour, the Lord Jesus

2410
03:10:58,076 --> 03:11:03,856
Christ, who will change the body of our
humiliation to be conformed to the body of his

2411
03:11:03,896 --> 03:11:10,236
glory, according to the working by which he
is able even to subject all things to himself.

2412
03:11:10,676 --> 03:11:12,996
Philippians, chapter four.

2413
03:11:13,036 --> 03:11:19,676
Therefore, my brothers, beloved and longed for, my
joy and crown, stand firm in the Lord

2414
03:11:19,716 --> 03:11:21,316
in this way, my beloved.

2415
03:11:22,176 --> 03:11:28,196
I exhort Euodia, and I exhort Syntyche, to
think the same way in the Lord.

2416
03:11:28,736 --> 03:11:35,216
Yes, I beg you also, true partner, help
these women, for they laboured with me

2417
03:11:35,256 --> 03:11:41,476
in the Good News with Clement also, and
the rest of my fellow workers, whose names are

2418
03:11:41,516 --> 03:11:42,416
in the book of life.

2419
03:11:43,436 --> 03:11:45,136
Rejoice in the Lord always!

2420
03:11:45,676 --> 03:11:47,516
Again I will say, “Rejoice!”

2421
03:11:48,496 --> 03:11:51,156
Let your gentleness be known to all men.

2422
03:11:51,736 --> 03:11:52,836
The Lord is at hand.

2423
03:11:53,676 --> 03:12:00,096
In nothing be anxious, but in everything,
by prayer and petition with thanksgiving, let

2424
03:12:00,136 --> 03:12:02,356
your requests be made known to God.

2425
03:12:02,396 --> 03:12:08,836
And the peace of God, which surpasses
all understanding, will guard your hearts and your

2426
03:12:08,876 --> 03:12:10,396
thoughts in Christ Jesus.

2427
03:12:10,996 --> 03:12:16,976
Finally, brothers, whatever things are
true, whatever things are honourable, whatever

2428
03:12:17,016 --> 03:12:23,616
things are just, whatever things are
pure, whatever things are lovely, whatever things

2429
03:12:23,656 --> 03:12:29,836
are of good report: if there is any virtue
and if there is anything worthy of praise,

2430
03:12:30,576 --> 03:12:31,876
think about these things.

2431
03:12:32,496 --> 03:12:38,676
Do the things which you learnt, received,
heard, and saw in me, and the God of peace

2432
03:12:38,716 --> 03:12:39,796
will be with you.

2433
03:12:40,616 --> 03:12:45,956
But I rejoice in the Lord greatly that
now at length you have revived your thought for

2434
03:12:45,996 --> 03:12:50,896
me; in which you did indeed take thought,
but you lacked opportunity.

2435
03:12:50,936 --> 03:12:57,656
Not that I speak because of lack, for I
have learnt in whatever state I am, to

2436
03:12:57,696 --> 03:12:58,816
be content in it.

2437
03:12:58,984 --> 03:13:02,824
I know how to be humbled, and I also know
how to abound.

2438
03:13:03,864 --> 03:13:09,904
In any and all circumstances I have learnt the
secret both to be filled and to be hungry,

2439
03:13:10,524 --> 03:13:13,284
both to abound and to be in need.

2440
03:13:14,224 --> 03:13:17,744
I can do all things through Christ who
strengthens me.

2441
03:13:18,084 --> 03:13:20,884
However you did well that you shared in my
affliction.

2442
03:13:21,704 --> 03:13:27,684
You yourselves also know, you Philippians, that
in the beginning of the Good News, when

2443
03:13:27,724 --> 03:13:33,884
I departed from Macedonia, no assembly shared with
me in the matter of giving and receiving

2444
03:13:34,304 --> 03:13:35,204
but you only.

2445
03:13:36,064 --> 03:13:40,124
For even in Thessalonica you sent once and
again to my need.

2446
03:13:40,704 --> 03:13:46,004
Not that I seek for the gift, but I
seek for the fruit that increases to your account.

2447
03:13:47,004 --> 03:13:48,744
But I have all things and abound.

2448
03:13:49,584 --> 03:13:56,724
I am filled, having received from Epaphroditus
the things that came from you, a sweet-smelling

2449
03:13:56,764 --> 03:14:01,124
fragrance, an acceptable and well-pleasing
sacrifice to God.

2450
03:14:01,764 --> 03:14:07,584
My God will supply every need of yours
according to his riches in glory in Christ Jesus.

2451
03:14:08,604 --> 03:14:13,064
Now to our God and Father be the glory
forever and ever!

2452
03:14:13,664 --> 03:14:14,564
Amen.

2453
03:14:14,804 --> 03:14:17,024
Greet every saint in Christ Jesus.

2454
03:14:17,464 --> 03:14:19,404
The brothers who are with me greet you.

2455
03:14:20,064 --> 03:14:24,304
All the saints greet you, especially those
who are of Caesar’s household.

2456
03:14:25,484 --> 03:14:28,824
The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ be with
you all.

2457
03:14:29,304 --> 03:14:30,124
Amen.

2458
03:14:30,164 --> 03:14:32,364
Daniel, chapter one.

2459
03:14:32,404 --> 03:14:38,844
In the third year of the reign of
Jehoiakim king of Judah, Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon

2460
03:14:39,244 --> 03:14:41,604
came to Jerusalem and besieged it.

2461
03:14:42,084 --> 03:14:48,044
The Lord gave Jehoiakim king of Judah into
his hand, with some of the vessels of the

2462
03:14:48,084 --> 03:14:53,944
house of God; and he carried them into the
land of Shinar to the house of his god.

2463
03:14:54,924 --> 03:14:58,144
He brought the vessels into the treasure
house of his god.

2464
03:14:58,538 --> 03:15:04,638
The king spoke to Ashpenaz, the master of
his eunuchs, that he should bring in some of

2465
03:15:04,678 --> 03:15:11,438
the children of Israel, even of the royal
offspring and of the nobles: youths

2466
03:15:11,479 --> 03:15:18,278
in whom was no defect, but well-favoured,
skilful in all wisdom, endowed with knowledge,

2467
03:15:18,958 --> 03:15:24,758
understanding science, and who had the ability
to stand in the king’s palace; and that

2468
03:15:24,798 --> 03:15:28,218
he should teach them the learning and the
language of the Chaldeans.

2469
03:15:28,838 --> 03:15:33,998
The king appointed for them a daily portion
of the king’s delicacies and of the wine

2470
03:15:34,038 --> 03:15:39,738
which he drank, and that they should be
nourished three years, that at its end they should

2471
03:15:39,778 --> 03:15:40,958
stand before the king.

2472
03:15:41,338 --> 03:15:48,178
Now amongst these of the children of
Judah were Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah.

2473
03:15:48,819 --> 03:15:55,138
The prince of the eunuchs gave names to
them: to Daniel he gave the name Belteshazzar;

2474
03:15:55,178 --> 03:16:02,098
to Hananiah, Shadrach; to Mishael,
Meshach; and to Azariah, Abednego.

2475
03:16:02,138 --> 03:16:08,118
But Daniel purposed in his heart that he
would not defile himself with the king’s delicacies,

2476
03:16:08,798 --> 03:16:10,378
nor with the wine which he drank.

2477
03:16:11,118 --> 03:16:15,878
Therefore he requested of the prince of
the eunuchs that he might not defile himself.

2478
03:16:16,938 --> 03:16:22,899
Now God made Daniel find kindness and compassion
in the sight of the prince of the eunuchs.

2479
03:16:23,938 --> 03:16:29,558
The prince of the eunuchs said to Daniel,
“I fear my lord the king, who has appointed

2480
03:16:29,598 --> 03:16:30,979
your food and your drink.

2481
03:16:31,618 --> 03:16:36,498
For why should he see your faces worse looking
than the youths who are of your own age?

2482
03:16:37,498 --> 03:16:39,899
Then you would endanger my head with the
king.”

2483
03:16:40,618 --> 03:16:45,338
Then Daniel said to the steward whom the
prince of the eunuchs had appointed over Daniel,

2484
03:16:45,378 --> 03:16:51,878
Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah: “Test your
servants, I beg you,

2485
03:16:52,239 --> 03:16:56,758
ten days; and let them give us vegetables
to eat and water to drink.

2486
03:16:57,458 --> 03:17:03,138
Then let our faces be examined before you,
and the face of the youths who eat of the

2487
03:17:03,178 --> 03:17:07,559
king’s delicacies; and as you see, deal
with your servants.”

2488
03:17:08,798 --> 03:17:13,118
So he listened to them in this matter, and
tested them for ten days.

2489
03:17:13,533 --> 03:17:19,733
At the end of ten days, their faces
appeared fairer and they were fatter in flesh than

2490
03:17:19,773 --> 03:17:22,573
all the youths who ate of the king’s
delicacies.

2491
03:17:23,493 --> 03:17:28,813
So the steward took away their delicacies and
the wine that they were given to drink,

2492
03:17:29,533 --> 03:17:30,433
and gave them vegetables.

2493
03:17:31,533 --> 03:17:37,373
Now as for these four youths, God gave
them knowledge and skill in all learning and wisdom;

2494
03:17:38,453 --> 03:17:41,553
and Daniel had understanding in all
visions and dreams.

2495
03:17:42,073 --> 03:17:46,973
At the end of the days which the king had
appointed for bringing them in, the prince

2496
03:17:47,013 --> 03:17:50,033
of the eunuchs brought them in before
Nebuchadnezzar.

2497
03:17:50,493 --> 03:17:57,393
The king talked with them; and amongst them
all was found no one like Daniel, Hananiah,

2498
03:17:57,433 --> 03:18:00,053
Mishael, and Azariah.

2499
03:18:00,093 --> 03:18:02,273
Therefore stood they before the king.

2500
03:18:02,793 --> 03:18:08,193
In every matter of wisdom and understanding
concerning which the king enquired of them,

2501
03:18:08,933 --> 03:18:14,533
he found them ten times better than all
the magicians and enchanters who were in all

2502
03:18:14,573 --> 03:18:15,473
his realm.

2503
03:18:16,453 --> 03:18:19,733
Daniel continued even to the first year of
King Cyrus.

2504
03:18:20,333 --> 03:18:22,413
Daniel, chapter two.

2505
03:18:22,453 --> 03:18:28,613
In the second year of the
reign of Nebuchadnezzar, Nebuchadnezzar dreamt dreams; and

2506
